{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430133965,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_lbeq60KIot7IdmHhqtd61512","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"CLAUDE_PID\\|process.ppid\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md .claude/settings.json | head -20; echo \"---REGISTRY---\"; grep -n \"session-relaunch\" -A4 .skilled/hooks/hook-registry.json | head -60"},"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:25:`skilled-loop` exports `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` with the selected runtime. It carries the first launch's model for every runtime. Pi and Hermes also carry their provider. Claude and Pi carry their name. Pi carries its extension flags. Relative Pi extension paths resolve against the wrapper's starting directory. `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can omit it and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. Other runtimes pass the id directly. Runtimes with no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse the value. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies Claude's process id only for the shell-child check. `complete` requires only the note path.\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:81:Prepare validates the note first. An invalid note exits 2. Outside `skilled-loop`, it prints a manual claim command and exits 3 without checking for running shell children. Inside the loop, a live child of the runtime process exits 2 when its command name is `sh`, `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `dash`, `ksh`, `mksh`, `tcsh`, `csh`, `nu` or `pwsh`. A leading `-` is stripped before that lookup, so a login shell still matches. Any other child program is not detected. The runtime pid comes from `CLAUDE_PID` when the variable is set. On runtimes without it, the check resolves the runtime as the direct child of the loop on prepare's ancestor chain. When no runtime resolves, it logs `running-work-check-skipped` and skips. A shell that is prepare's own ancestor does not count. `--runtime` must name one of Claude, Pi, OpenCode, Codex, Cursor, Hermes or Devin. Outside `skilled-loop` it overrides the environment or Claude default. Inside the loop, a supplied value must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. The nudge includes the selected runtime in its prepare command. A successful prepare writes a pending record and exits 0. At the hop cap it writes no record, prints the hop-limit line with the manual claim command and exits 3.\n---REGISTRY---\ngrep: .skilled/hooks/hook-registry.json: No such file or directory\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:25:`skilled-loop` exports `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` with the selected runtime. It carries the first launch's model for every runtime. Pi and Hermes also carry their provider. Claude and Pi carry their name. Pi carries its extension flags. Relative Pi extension paths resolve against the wrapper's starting directory. `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can omit it and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. Other runtimes pass the id directly. Runtimes with no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse the value. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies Claude's process id only for the shell-child check. `complete` requires only the note path.\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:81:Prepare validates the note first. An invalid note exits 2. Outside `skilled-loop`, it prints a manual claim command and exits 3 without checking for running shell children. Inside the loop, a live child of the runtime process exits 2 when its command name is `sh`, `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `dash`, `ksh`, `mksh`, `tcsh`, `csh`, `nu` or `pwsh`. A leading `-` is stripped before that lookup, so a login shell still matches. Any other child program is not detected. The runtime pid comes from `CLAUDE_PID` when the variable is set. On runtimes without it, the check resolves the runtime as the direct child of the loop on prepare's ancestor chain. When no runtime resolves, it logs `running-work-check-skipped` and skips. A shell that is prepare's own ancestor does not count. `--runtime` must name one of Claude, Pi, OpenCode, Codex, Cursor, Hermes or Devin. Outside `skilled-loop` it overrides the environment or Claude default. Inside the loop, a supplied value must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. The nudge includes the selected runtime in its prepare command. A successful prepare writes a pending record and exits 0. At the hop cap it writes no record, prints the hop-limit line with the manual claim command and exits 3.\n---REGISTRY---\ngrep: .skilled/hooks/hook-registry.json: No such file or directory\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"CLAUDE_PID\\|process.ppid\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md .claude/settings.json | head -20; echo \"---REGISTRY---\"; grep -n \"session-relaunch\" -A4 .skilled/hooks/hook-registry.json | head -60","time":{"start":1792430133934,"end":1792430133964}},"id":"prt_15529517c001ktjSQOq05fXYco","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552931af001V2jGdDhxEPW1ua"}}
