{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792430242965,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"id":"prt_1552afc94001Y0ZYGuX4n52WLN","messageID":"msg_1552af06d001yHKqFngz652MSL","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","snapshot":"cbc33b10a414b68ce649248c80cb6397b08e4557","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430252137,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_1oBGCZegjQgX5QjTRkiA7984","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"cache_read\\|cache_creation\\|input_tokens\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md | head -20; echo \"---tests---\"; grep -n \"resolveWindow\\|subdir\\|nested\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/tests/context-usage.test.cjs | head -30"},"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:29:Codex binds three repo hooks rendered from `hook-registry.json` into [.codex/hooks.json](../../../.codex/hooks.json). `prompt-seed.mjs` binds `UserPromptSubmit`: a `[session-relaunch]` prompt receives the claim-seed instructions, and a non-seed prompt runs the same threshold check as `context-nudge.mjs`, which binds `PostToolUse`. The Codex hook installer allows each script under one event only, so seed detection and the mid-session nudge are separate entry points over `shared.mjs`. The fill comes from the transcript rollout's latest `token_count` event: `last_token_usage.input_tokens` is the numerator and `cached_input_tokens` stays out because it is already inside that count. The window is `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, then the event's `model_context_window`. The nudge reaches the model as `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, the envelope the repo's other Codex adapters emit. `stop-arm.mjs` accepts only payloads whose `hook_event_name` is `Stop`. It resolves the target, arms a matching pending record, then spawns the killer with `--transcript <transcript_path>`. A spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next Stop restarts its killer. Codex exports no pid variable, so the killer target resolves through the same ancestor rule the CLI's running-work check uses. `skilled-loop codex` always starts Codex with `--no-daemon` because its shared app-server daemon keeps the environment of the session that started it. In a git worktree, Codex reads its `hooks.json` from the main checkout, not the worktree. The automatic hop needs the session-relaunch rows in the main checkout's file. Each of those three rows, like the three session-relaunch rows in the Claude settings file, carries the repo's hook-drift fallback: a missing adapter prints a `mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<script>` line on stderr and still returns an envelope the host accepts. Claude's fallback adds `mkHookDrift: true`. Codex omits that key, because it rejects unknown keys, and answers its Stop event with `systemMessage` instead of `hookSpecificOutput`, because it rejects that envelope on Stop.\n---tests---\n13:  resolveWindow,\n66:test('resolveWindow gives SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS precedence over settings', (t) => {\n73:    resolveWindow({\n83:test('resolveWindow prefers settings.local.json over project and home settings', (t) => {\n89:    resolveWindow({\n99:test('resolveWindow uses project settings.json before the home setting', (t) => {\n104:    resolveWindow({\n114:test('resolveWindow treats settings read errors as absent', (t) => {\n132:    resolveWindow({\n142:test('resolveWindow falls back to the home Claude setting', (t) => {\n146:    resolveWindow({\n156:test('resolveWindow selects a one-million-token window for a model containing [1m]', (t) => {\n159:    resolveWindow({\n169:test('resolveWindow defaults to a 200000-token window', (t) => {\n172:    resolveWindow({\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:29:Codex binds three repo hooks rendered from `hook-registry.json` into [.codex/hooks.json](../../../.codex/hooks.json). `prompt-seed.mjs` binds `UserPromptSubmit`: a `[session-relaunch]` prompt receives the claim-seed instructions, and a non-seed prompt runs the same threshold check as `context-nudge.mjs`, which binds `PostToolUse`. The Codex hook installer allows each script under one event only, so seed detection and the mid-session nudge are separate entry points over `shared.mjs`. The fill comes from the transcript rollout's latest `token_count` event: `last_token_usage.input_tokens` is the numerator and `cached_input_tokens` stays out because it is already inside that count. The window is `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, then the event's `model_context_window`. The nudge reaches the model as `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, the envelope the repo's other Codex adapters emit. `stop-arm.mjs` accepts only payloads whose `hook_event_name` is `Stop`. It resolves the target, arms a matching pending record, then spawns the killer with `--transcript <transcript_path>`. A spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next Stop restarts its killer. Codex exports no pid variable, so the killer target resolves through the same ancestor rule the CLI's running-work check uses. `skilled-loop codex` always starts Codex with `--no-daemon` because its shared app-server daemon keeps the environment of the session that started it. In a git worktree, Codex reads its `hooks.json` from the main checkout, not the worktree. The automatic hop needs the session-relaunch rows in the main checkout's file. Each of those three rows, like the three session-relaunch rows in the Claude settings file, carries the repo's hook-drift fallback: a missing adapter prints a `mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<script>` line on stderr and still returns an envelope the host accepts. Claude's fallback adds `mkHookDrift: true`. Codex omits that key, because it rejects unknown keys, and answers its Stop event with `systemMessage` instead of `hookSpecificOutput`, because it rejects that envelope on Stop.\n---tests---\n13:  resolveWindow,\n66:test('resolveWindow gives SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS precedence over settings', (t) => {\n73:    resolveWindow({\n83:test('resolveWindow prefers settings.local.json over project and home settings', (t) => {\n89:    resolveWindow({\n99:test('resolveWindow uses project settings.json before the home setting', (t) => {\n104:    resolveWindow({\n114:test('resolveWindow treats settings read errors as absent', (t) => {\n132:    resolveWindow({\n142:test('resolveWindow falls back to the home Claude setting', (t) => {\n146:    resolveWindow({\n156:test('resolveWindow selects a one-million-token window for a model containing [1m]', (t) => {\n159:    resolveWindow({\n169:test('resolveWindow defaults to a 200000-token window', (t) => {\n172:    resolveWindow({\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"cache_read\\|cache_creation\\|input_tokens\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md | head -20; echo \"---tests---\"; grep -n \"resolveWindow\\|subdir\\|nested\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/tests/context-usage.test.cjs | head -30","time":{"start":1792430252113,"end":1792430252136}},"id":"prt_1552b1f06001POCEUj3Nfwg2cZ","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552af06d001yHKqFngz652MSL"}}
