{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430352935,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_I5TskUHcXdWS4avyjc7N5918","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,160p .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/codex/shared.mjs"},"output":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Codex Shared Session Relaunch Adapter\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { readStdin, parseJsonFailOpen } from '../../shared/hook-adapter-shared.cjs';\nimport {\n  configPath,\n  isHookEnabled,\n  loadConfigFile,\n} from '../../shared/hook-flags.mjs';\nimport { appendLog } from '../lib/relaunch-core.cjs';\nimport {\n  fillRatio,\n  readCodexUsage,\n  resolveCodexWindow,\n} from '../lib/context-usage.cjs';\nimport nudge from '../lib/nudge.cjs';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst CONCERN = 'session-relaunch';\nconst CLI_COMMAND = 'node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction done() {\n  process.exit(0);\n}\n\nfunction emit(eventName, text) {\n  const envelope = {\n    hookSpecificOutput: {\n      hookEventName: eventName,\n      additionalContext: text,\n    },\n  };\n  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(envelope), done);\n}\n\nfunction logEvent(event, fields) {\n  try {\n    appendLog(event, fields, process.env);\n  } catch {}\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. CORE LOGIC\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync function main(expectedEvent) {\n  const config = loadConfigFile(configPath());\n  let enabled = false;\n  try {\n    enabled = isHookEnabled(CONCERN, process.env, config);\n  } catch {}\n  if (!enabled) return done();\n\n  const payload = parseJsonFailOpen(await readStdin());\n  if (payload === null || typeof payload !== 'object') return done();\n\n  const eventName = payload.hook_event_name;\n  if (eventName !== expectedEvent) return done();\n\n  const sessionId = payload.session_id;\n  if (!nudge.validSessionId(sessionId)) return done();\n\n  if (eventName === 'UserPromptSubmit' && nudge.isSeedPrompt(payload.prompt)) {\n    return emit(eventName, nudge.seedText({\n      notePath: nudge.notePathFromSeed(payload.prompt) ?? '<handoff-path>',\n      specFolder: nudge.specFolderFromSeed(payload.prompt),\n      sessionId,\n      cliPath: CLI_COMMAND,\n    }));\n  }\n\n  if (typeof payload.transcript_path !== 'string' || !payload.transcript_path) {\n    return done();\n  }\n\n  let usage;\n  let windowTokens;\n  try {\n    usage = readCodexUsage(payload.transcript_path);\n    if (usage === null) return done();\n    windowTokens = resolveCodexWindow(usage.modelContextWindow, process.env);\n    if (windowTokens === null) return done();\n  } catch (error) {\n    logEvent('context-nudge-error', { stage: 'usage', message: error.message });\n    return done();\n  }\n\n  const ratio = fillRatio(usage.fillTokens, windowTokens);\n  const threshold = nudge.relaunchThreshold(config);\n  if (ratio < threshold) return done();\n\n  // A prepared or armed record means this session already ran the handoff steps.\n  if (nudge.handoffPending({ sessionId })) return done();\n  // A session at its hop cap cannot relaunch, so these steps would prepare nothing.\n  if (nudge.hopLimitReached()) return done();\n\n  const decision = nudge.nextLevel({\n    ratio,\n    threshold,\n    state: nudge.readState(sessionId),\n  });\n  if (!decision.nudge) return done();\n\n  const notePath = nudge.plannedNotePath({ cwd: payload.cwd, sessionId });\n  try {\n    nudge.writeState(sessionId, decision.level);\n  } catch (error) {\n    logEvent('context-nudge-error', { stage: 'state', message: error.message });\n  }\n  return emit(eventName, nudge.handoffText({\n    notePath,\n    sessionId,\n    specFolder: payload.spec_folder,\n    runtime: 'codex',\n    cliPath: CLI_COMMAND,\n    cwd: payload.cwd || process.cwd(),\n    ratio,\n  }));\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 5. EXPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Run the shared prompt logic for one registered Codex hook event.\n *\n * @param {string} expectedEvent - The event handled by the calling entrypoint.\n */\nexport function runCodexAdapter(expectedEvent) {\n  main(expectedEvent).catch(done);\n}\n","metadata":{"output":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Codex Shared Session Relaunch Adapter\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { readStdin, parseJsonFailOpen } from '../../shared/hook-adapter-shared.cjs';\nimport {\n  configPath,\n  isHookEnabled,\n  loadConfigFile,\n} from '../../shared/hook-flags.mjs';\nimport { appendLog } from '../lib/relaunch-core.cjs';\nimport {\n  fillRatio,\n  readCodexUsage,\n  resolveCodexWindow,\n} from '../lib/context-usage.cjs';\nimport nudge from '../lib/nudge.cjs';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst CONCERN = 'session-relaunch';\nconst CLI_COMMAND = 'node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction done() {\n  process.exit(0);\n}\n\nfunction emit(eventName, text) {\n  const envelope = {\n    hookSpecificOutput: {\n      hookEventName: eventName,\n      additionalContext: text,\n    },\n  };\n  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(envelope), done);\n}\n\nfunction logEvent(event, fields) {\n  try {\n    appendLog(event, fields, process.env);\n  } catch {}\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. CORE LOGIC\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync function main(expectedEvent) {\n  const config = loadConfigFile(configPath());\n  let enabled = false;\n  try {\n    enabled = isHookEnabled(CONCERN, process.env, config);\n  } catch {}\n  if (!enabled) return done();\n\n  const payload = parseJsonFailOpen(await readStdin());\n  if (payload === null || typeof payload !== 'object') return done();\n\n  const eventName = payload.hook_event_name;\n  if (eventName !== expectedEvent) return done();\n\n  const sessionId = payload.session_id;\n  if (!nudge.validSessionId(sessionId)) return done();\n\n  if (eventName === 'UserPromptSubmit' && nudge.isSeedPrompt(payload.prompt)) {\n    return emit(eventName, nudge.seedText({\n      notePath: nudge.notePathFromSeed(payload.prompt) ?? '<handoff-path>',\n      specFolder: nudge.specFolderFromSeed(payload.prompt),\n      sessionId,\n      cliPath: CLI_COMMAND,\n    }));\n  }\n\n  if (typeof payload.transcript_path !== 'string' || !payload.transcript_path) {\n    return done();\n  }\n\n  let usage;\n  let windowTokens;\n  try {\n    usage = readCodexUsage(payload.transcript_path);\n    if (usage === null) return done();\n    windowTokens = resolveCodexWindow(usage.modelContextWindow, process.env);\n    if (windowTokens === null) return done();\n  } catch (error) {\n    logEvent('context-nudge-error', { stage: 'usage', message: error.message });\n    return done();\n  }\n\n  const ratio = fillRatio(usage.fillTokens, windowTokens);\n  const threshold = nudge.relaunchThreshold(config);\n  if (ratio < threshold) return done();\n\n  // A prepared or armed record means this session already ran the handoff steps.\n  if (nudge.handoffPending({ sessionId })) return done();\n  // A session at its hop cap cannot relaunch, so these steps would prepare nothing.\n  if (nudge.hopLimitReached()) return done();\n\n  const decision = nudge.nextLevel({\n    ratio,\n    threshold,\n    state: nudge.readState(sessionId),\n  });\n  if (!decision.nudge) return done();\n\n  const notePath = nudge.plannedNotePath({ cwd: payload.cwd, sessionId });\n  try {\n    nudge.writeState(sessionId, decision.level);\n  } catch (error) {\n    logEvent('context-nudge-error', { stage: 'state', message: error.message });\n  }\n  return emit(eventName, nudge.handoffText({\n    notePath,\n    sessionId,\n    specFolder: payload.spec_folder,\n    runtime: 'codex',\n    cliPath: CLI_COMMAND,\n    cwd: payload.cwd || process.cwd(),\n    ratio,\n  }));\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 5. EXPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Run the shared prompt logic for one registered Codex hook event.\n *\n * @param {string} expectedEvent - The event handled by the calling entrypoint.\n */\nexport function runCodexAdapter(expectedEvent) {\n  main(expectedEvent).catch(done);\n}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"sed -n 1,160p .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/codex/shared.mjs","time":{"start":1792430352923,"end":1792430352934}},"id":"prt_1552ca9b0001zm3ywl16yxENCH","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552c8c76001f4BwjQJ6CY1bvI"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430414828,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_NbYQCsnylU4oqa1GCrFW3176","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER\" .skilled .opencode opencode.json 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -20; echo \"---HERMES---\"; grep -rn \"HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER\" .skilled | head -10"},"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:338:        specFolder: process.env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER || undefined,\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:34:  'SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER',\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:68:  delete process.env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:289:  it('includes the save step when SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER is unset', async () => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:332:    process.env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER = 'specs/from-environment';\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:113:| `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER` | (unset) | string (repo-relative packet path) | Spec packet the session is bound to. The Cursor spec-gate prebind satisfies Gate 3 from it at session start, and the Pi extension and the OpenCode plugin write it into a planned handoff note's `spec_folder` so the relaunched session resumes that packet. Claude and Codex take `spec_folder` from the hook payload instead. | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/`, `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/`, `.opencode/plugins/session-relaunch.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:114:| `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` | (unset) | string (repo-relative packet path) | The Hermes form of `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER`. The repo-guards plugin reads the bound packet's goal from it and passes it to the relaunch nudge as the payload's `spec_folder`. | `.hermes/plugins/repo-guards/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-claude.test.mjs:42:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/README.md:72:| Environment | `isolatedEnv()` deletes `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER` and the gate flags before each spawn, so the host environment cannot change a result. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-codex.test.mjs:42:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-devin.test.mjs:40:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:56:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:117:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:124:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:153:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:201:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: invalidFolder,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:207:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: invalidFolder,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:305:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/README.md:72:Cursor's generic `preToolUse` event covers shell and file-write calls, so `spec-gate-enforce.mjs` is wired there rather than `beforeShellExecution` (which only covers shell and would miss `Write` entirely). `beforeSubmitPrompt` remains registered but has not fired under the installed CLI; `spec-gate-prebind.mjs` therefore uses confirmed `sessionStart` delivery to satisfy a validated `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER` or open state only when `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=1` is explicitly set for an identifiable top-level session. A dispatched/child session (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`) is a complete Gate-3 no-op enforced in the shared core. Both spec-gate adapters resolve `workspace_roots[0]` only, so multi-root Cursor workspaces are not enforced against secondary roots.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-prebind.mjs:12:// 1. SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER names a valid spec folder up front: satisfy the gate\n---HERMES---\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:114:| `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` | (unset) | string (repo-relative packet path) | The Hermes form of `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER`. The repo-guards plugin reads the bound packet's goal from it and passes it to the relaunch nudge as the payload's `spec_folder`. | `.hermes/plugins/repo-guards/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/shims/adapter-shim-core.cjs:62:        HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER: process.env.HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER || null,\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:291:        expect(typeof captures[0].env.HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER).toBe('string');\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:292:        expect(captures[0].env.HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER).not.toBe('');\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2807:const HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER_ENV = 'HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER';\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3498:          [HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER_ENV]: specFolder,\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4040:  HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER_ENV,\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-second-pass/findings-and-recommendations.md:27:- **Fix as landed**: with `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` set, the plugin appends `Bound packet: <path>` plus the packet goal's durable slice to the section.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/feature-catalog/runtime-surface/repo-guards-project-plugin.md:26:The plugin manifest declares six hooks and the registration function registers exactly those six: pre-llm-call, pre-tool-call, transform-tool-result, pre-verify, session-start and session-end, plus four system-prompt sections. Together they bridge every repo hook core Hermes's plugin API can reach: the skill advisor and the spec-gate classification at prompt time (the gate's question itself is delivered once, at the first write); the spec-gate enforcement, dispatch preflint, task-dispatch guard, MCP route guard, sk-git advisory and sk-vision core before a tool call; the gate notice and post-edit quality on a write result; the shared goal core at session start; the worktree, dist-freshness, git-hooks and primary-reconcile guards as a session section; and session cleanup at session end. The pre-tool-call hook also refuses the write and command tools when the runner marks a leaf read-only (`SPECKIT_HERMES_READ_ONLY`), because Hermes has no read-only file toolset, blocks a write the enforced spec gate has not been bound for yet, and stages the sk-git advisory for a git-shaped command, which the transform-tool-result hook appends to that command's result. Three system-prompt sections, each under Hermes's 4000-character cap, carry the session-start context, the persona binding (`HERMES_AGENT_PERSONA=<name>` points the session at the preloaded `agent-<name>` skill) and, when `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` names a packet, the goal brief the shared goal core renders for that packet once it is bound to the session. The pre-tool-call hook runs the dispatch preflight core against the command a tool call is about to run, and separately refuses a nested Hermes dispatch launched from inside a Hermes session, on the same reasoning the packet gives for its self-invocation guard. For a command naming `git` or `gh` it then runs the sk-git message gate, which blocks a `git commit` message, `gh pr` description or new branch name that breaks the repository's own sk-git templates; a gate that cannot run allows the call, because the git hooks and CI enforce the same rules. The pre-verify hook runs the completion-evidence core, which blocks a completion claim naming no evidence. The session-end hook records the closing state through the shared lifecycle core.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/references/hook-contract.md:42:| `on_session_start` | shared goal core | Binds the packet named by `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` to the session id |\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:338:        specFolder: process.env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER || undefined,\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:34:  'SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER',\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:68:  delete process.env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:289:  it('includes the save step when SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER is unset', async () => {\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:332:    process.env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER = 'specs/from-environment';\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:113:| `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER` | (unset) | string (repo-relative packet path) | Spec packet the session is bound to. The Cursor spec-gate prebind satisfies Gate 3 from it at session start, and the Pi extension and the OpenCode plugin write it into a planned handoff note's `spec_folder` so the relaunched session resumes that packet. Claude and Codex take `spec_folder` from the hook payload instead. | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/`, `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/`, `.opencode/plugins/session-relaunch.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:114:| `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` | (unset) | string (repo-relative packet path) | The Hermes form of `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER`. The repo-guards plugin reads the bound packet's goal from it and passes it to the relaunch nudge as the payload's `spec_folder`. | `.hermes/plugins/repo-guards/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-claude.test.mjs:42:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/README.md:72:| Environment | `isolatedEnv()` deletes `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER` and the gate flags before each spawn, so the host environment cannot change a result. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-codex.test.mjs:42:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-devin.test.mjs:40:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:56:  delete env.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:117:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:124:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:153:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:201:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: invalidFolder,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:207:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: invalidFolder,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-prebind.test.mjs:305:      SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER: folderRel,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/README.md:72:Cursor's generic `preToolUse` event covers shell and file-write calls, so `spec-gate-enforce.mjs` is wired there rather than `beforeShellExecution` (which only covers shell and would miss `Write` entirely). `beforeSubmitPrompt` remains registered but has not fired under the installed CLI; `spec-gate-prebind.mjs` therefore uses confirmed `sessionStart` delivery to satisfy a validated `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER` or open state only when `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=1` is explicitly set for an identifiable top-level session. A dispatched/child session (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`) is a complete Gate-3 no-op enforced in the shared core. Both spec-gate adapters resolve `workspace_roots[0]` only, so multi-root Cursor workspaces are not enforced against secondary roots.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/cursor/spec-gate-prebind.mjs:12:// 1. SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER names a valid spec folder up front: satisfy the gate\n---HERMES---\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:114:| `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` | (unset) | string (repo-relative packet path) | The Hermes form of `SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER`. The repo-guards plugin reads the bound packet's goal from it and passes it to the relaunch nudge as the payload's `spec_folder`. | `.hermes/plugins/repo-guards/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/shims/adapter-shim-core.cjs:62:        HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER: process.env.HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER || null,\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:291:        expect(typeof captures[0].env.HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER).toBe('string');\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:292:        expect(captures[0].env.HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER).not.toBe('');\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2807:const HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER_ENV = 'HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER';\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3498:          [HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER_ENV]: specFolder,\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4040:  HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER_ENV,\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-second-pass/findings-and-recommendations.md:27:- **Fix as landed**: with `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` set, the plugin appends `Bound packet: <path>` plus the packet goal's durable slice to the section.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/feature-catalog/runtime-surface/repo-guards-project-plugin.md:26:The plugin manifest declares six hooks and the registration function registers exactly those six: pre-llm-call, pre-tool-call, transform-tool-result, pre-verify, session-start and session-end, plus four system-prompt sections. Together they bridge every repo hook core Hermes's plugin API can reach: the skill advisor and the spec-gate classification at prompt time (the gate's question itself is delivered once, at the first write); the spec-gate enforcement, dispatch preflint, task-dispatch guard, MCP route guard, sk-git advisory and sk-vision core before a tool call; the gate notice and post-edit quality on a write result; the shared goal core at session start; the worktree, dist-freshness, git-hooks and primary-reconcile guards as a session section; and session cleanup at session end. The pre-tool-call hook also refuses the write and command tools when the runner marks a leaf read-only (`SPECKIT_HERMES_READ_ONLY`), because Hermes has no read-only file toolset, blocks a write the enforced spec gate has not been bound for yet, and stages the sk-git advisory for a git-shaped command, which the transform-tool-result hook appends to that command's result. Three system-prompt sections, each under Hermes's 4000-character cap, carry the session-start context, the persona binding (`HERMES_AGENT_PERSONA=<name>` points the session at the preloaded `agent-<name>` skill) and, when `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` names a packet, the goal brief the shared goal core renders for that packet once it is bound to the session. The pre-tool-call hook runs the dispatch preflight core against the command a tool call is about to run, and separately refuses a nested Hermes dispatch launched from inside a Hermes session, on the same reasoning the packet gives for its self-invocation guard. For a command naming `git` or `gh` it then runs the sk-git message gate, which blocks a `git commit` message, `gh pr` description or new branch name that breaks the repository's own sk-git templates; a gate that cannot run allows the call, because the git hooks and CI enforce the same rules. The pre-verify hook runs the completion-evidence core, which blocks a completion claim naming no evidence. The session-end hook records the closing state through the shared lifecycle core.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/references/hook-contract.md:42:| `on_session_start` | shared goal core | Binds the packet named by `HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER` to the session id |\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER\" .skilled .opencode opencode.json 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -20; echo \"---HERMES---\"; grep -rn \"HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER\" .skilled | head -10","time":{"start":1792430352789,"end":1792430414826}},"id":"prt_1552ca8d0001jjTEEOJxTybubp","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552c8c76001f4BwjQJ6CY1bvI"}}
