{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430454506,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_zlYKJ6rtKReqsqKuXQ5N7610","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"process.pid\\|server process\\|plugin\" .opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs | head -20; echo \"---DOCS---\"; grep -rn \"OpenCode plugin\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md | head -10"},"output":".opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:16:const PLUGIN_PATH = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled', 'plugins', 'session-relaunch.js');\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:163:test('hook flags written after plugin load silence the next event', async (t) => {\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:417:test('a restarted plugin repeats its persisted nudge at the threshold', async (t) => {\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:916:  assert.ok(args.includes(String(process.pid)));\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:950:    `${process.pid} ${new Date().toISOString()}\\n`,\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:1172:test('malformed plugin events and transforms never throw', async (t) => {\n---DOCS---\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:97:The killer polls transcript mtime every 100 ms. When the transcript stays unchanged for `--idle-ms` (3000 ms by default), it confirms the target is a descendant of the loop and re-reads the record. It sends SIGTERM only when the record is still armed and below the hop cap. At or above the cap it unarms the record with reason `hop-cap`, logs `killer-hop-cap` and sends neither a signal nor a notification. The OpenCode plugin runs on Bun, so it starts the killer with `node` instead of `process.execPath`, which points to the OpenCode CLI. The `--loop-id` value must be greater than 1. If the record is no longer armed, the killer logs `killer-no-armed-record`. If the target exits during the SIGTERM call, it logs `target-gone`.\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:164:The killer CLI requires `--loop-id` and `--target-pid`. `--transcript` is optional: the Claude and Codex Stop hooks and the Pi arm pass it (Pi passes its session file when the path resolves). The Hermes arm and the OpenCode plugin do not. Without it, idle means the configured idle time has elapsed since the killer started. The loop id must be greater than 1 and match `SKILLED_LOOP_ID`. The defaults are `--idle-ms 3000` and `--timeout-ms 30000`. The killer polls every 100 ms. `--no-notify` defaults to off. Without it, a timeout attempts a notification. The Stop hook starts the killer without `--no-notify`.\n","metadata":{"output":".opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:16:const PLUGIN_PATH = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled', 'plugins', 'session-relaunch.js');\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:163:test('hook flags written after plugin load silence the next event', async (t) => {\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:417:test('a restarted plugin repeats its persisted nudge at the threshold', async (t) => {\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:916:  assert.ok(args.includes(String(process.pid)));\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:950:    `${process.pid} ${new Date().toISOString()}\\n`,\n.opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:1172:test('malformed plugin events and transforms never throw', async (t) => {\n---DOCS---\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:97:The killer polls transcript mtime every 100 ms. When the transcript stays unchanged for `--idle-ms` (3000 ms by default), it confirms the target is a descendant of the loop and re-reads the record. It sends SIGTERM only when the record is still armed and below the hop cap. At or above the cap it unarms the record with reason `hop-cap`, logs `killer-hop-cap` and sends neither a signal nor a notification. The OpenCode plugin runs on Bun, so it starts the killer with `node` instead of `process.execPath`, which points to the OpenCode CLI. The `--loop-id` value must be greater than 1. If the record is no longer armed, the killer logs `killer-no-armed-record`. If the target exits during the SIGTERM call, it logs `target-gone`.\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:164:The killer CLI requires `--loop-id` and `--target-pid`. `--transcript` is optional: the Claude and Codex Stop hooks and the Pi arm pass it (Pi passes its session file when the path resolves). The Hermes arm and the OpenCode plugin do not. Without it, idle means the configured idle time has elapsed since the killer started. The loop id must be greater than 1 and match `SKILLED_LOOP_ID`. The defaults are `--idle-ms 3000` and `--timeout-ms 30000`. The killer polls every 100 ms. `--no-notify` defaults to off. Without it, a timeout attempts a notification. The Stop hook starts the killer without `--no-notify`.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"process.pid\\|server process\\|plugin\" .opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs | head -20; echo \"---DOCS---\"; grep -rn \"OpenCode plugin\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md | head -10","time":{"start":1792430454484,"end":1792430454506}},"id":"prt_1552e35da001xVZxENm4E0n0lx","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552e164b001Cj6pI5hqYcEuu5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430454734,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_hDWDRJlkuzHosrZYzIi56527","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"test(\" .opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs | head -40; echo \"---PI TESTS---\"; grep -n \"it(\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts | head -40"},"output":"149:test('kill switch stops an active OpenCode nudge', async (t) => {\n163:test('hook flags written after plugin load silence the next event', async (t) => {\n186:test('active nudge appears on three consecutive system transforms', async (t) => {\n205:test('a five-point re-nudge replaces active text and keeps its note path', async (t) => {\n226:test('OpenCode nudge includes the save step when SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER is unset', async (t) => {\n250:test('outside a loop, active nudge stops after its planned note file appears', async (t) => {\n271:test('loop nudge continues after its handoff file exists without a relaunch record', async (t) => {\n279:test('loop nudge stops for matching pending and armed records', async (t) => {\n297:test('a usage above threshold queues no nudge while this session has a prepared handoff', async (t) => {\n321:test('a hop count at the cap queues no nudge', async (t) => {\n338:test('a stale armed record no longer suppresses the loop nudge', async (t) => {\n360:test('a zero max age makes any armed record stale for the nudge check', async (t) => {\n379:test('loop nudge continues for a record owned by another session', async (t) => {\n396:test('kill switch suppresses an in-loop nudge before handoff preparation', async (t) => {\n405:test('an active nudge is not injected into another session', async (t) => {\n417:test('a restarted plugin repeats its persisted nudge at the threshold', async (t) => {\n433:test('a restarted nudge reuses a matching handoff note', async (t) => {\n477:test('a restarted nudge ignores a closed handoff note and plans a fresh path', async (t) => {\n506:test('SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS overrides the model window', async (t) => {\n525:test('seed stays pending across later text parts', async (t) => {\n566:test('OpenCode uses the carried spec folder and keeps the suffixed note path intact', async (t) => {\n605:test('the seed repeats on every transform until the note is closed', async (t) => {\n643:test('a claimed note pushes one completion reminder instead of the claim text', async (t) => {\n684:test('a done note clears the seed and pushes nothing', async (t) => {\n719:test('a repeated seed message update keeps the seed while a new user message clears it', async (t) => {\n752:test('a different user message clears the pending seed', async (t) => {\n781:test('interleaved sessions keep their own seed and nudge text', async (t) => {\n832:test('recently active session survives the session-state cap', async (t) => {\n890:test(\n924:test(\n958:test('session.idle uses node under Bun and ignores killer spawn errors', async (t) => {\n991:test('session.idle logs a killer spawn error and leaves the record armed', async (t) => {\n1019:test('session.idle logs a synchronous killer spawn throw and leaves the record armed', async (t) => {\n1053:test('the planned note path lands under the env repo root, not the session directory', async (t) => {\n1075:test('a relative SESSION_RELAUNCH_REPO_ROOT still yields an absolute planned note path', async (t) => {\n1098:test('an invalid env threshold never falls through to the config file', async (t) => {\n1114:test('a seed path with a literal backslash round-trips unchanged', async (t) => {\n1140:test('a relative or untrimmed seed path falls back to the placeholder', async (t) => {\n1172:test('malformed plugin events and transforms never throw', async (t) => {\n---PI TESTS---\n82:async function emit(handlers: Map<string, Handler>, name: string, event: unknown, ctx: unknown) {\n98:  it('kill switch silences the extension', async () => {\n103:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n109:  it('reads the hook flags file again for each event', async () => {\n115:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n122:  it('uses the session window override instead of the runtime window', async () => {\n128:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n135:  it('message_end below the threshold does nothing', async () => {\n139:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n145:  it('message_end does nothing while this session already has a prepared handoff', async () => {\n160:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n168:  it('keeps the agent quiet at the hop limit', async () => {\n176:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n179:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n184:  it('retires a held nudge once the hop count reaches the cap before delivery', async () => {\n190:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n195:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n200:  it('agent_end delivers the nudge held from message_end exactly once', async () => {\n206:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n211:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n216:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n220:  it('agent_end stays quiet when the prepare call left a pending handoff', async () => {\n228:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n239:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n244:  it(\n251:      await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n254:      await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n255:      await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n258:      await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n259:      await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n262:      await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, ctx);\n273:  it('delivers the nudge without waiting for an operator turn', async () => {\n278:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n283:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, makeContext());\n289:  it('includes the save step when SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER is unset', async () => {\n294:    await emit(handlers, 'message_end', {\n297:    await emit(handlers, 'agent_end', {}, makeContext());\n314:  it('injects seedText in before_agent_start for a relaunch seed prompt', async () => {\n318:    const result = await emit(handlers, 'before_agent_start', {\n330:  it('uses the carried spec folder and keeps the suffixed note path intact', async () => {\n","metadata":{"output":"149:test('kill switch stops an active OpenCode nudge', async (t) => {\n163:test('hook flags written after plugin load silence the next event', async (t) => {\n186:test('active nudge appears on three consecutive system transforms', async (t) => {\n205:test('a five-point re-nudge replaces active text and keeps its note path', async (t) => {\n226:test('OpenCode nudge includes the save step when SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER is unset', async (t) => {\n250:test('outside a loop, active nudge stops after its planned note file appears', async (t) => {\n271:test('loop nudge continues after its handoff file exists without a relaunch record', async (t) => {\n279:test('loop nudge stops for matching pending and armed records', async (t) => {\n297:test('a usage above threshold queues no nudge while this session has a prepared handoff', async (t) => {\n321:test('a hop count at the cap queues no nudge', async (t) => {\n338:test('a stale armed record no longer suppresses the loop nudge', async (t) => {\n360:test('a zero max age makes any armed record stale for the nudge check', async (t) => {\n379:test('loop nudge continues for a record owned by another session', async (t) => {\n396:test('kill switch suppresses an in-loop nudge before handoff preparation', async (t) => {\n405:test('an active nudge is not injected into another session', async (t) => {\n417:test('a restarted plugin repeats its persisted nudge at the threshold', async (t) => {\n433:test('a restarted nudge reuses a matching handoff note', async (t) => {\n477:test('a restarted nudge ignores a closed handoff note and plans a fresh path', async (t) => {\n506:test('SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDO