{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430567714,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_tLh9yxn844jn3nSuDa5j2930","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json; echo \"---TEMPLATE---\"; sed -n 1,80p .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md"},"output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"./command-contract.schema.json\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"purpose\": \"Single machine-readable source of behavioral truth for the six router-shaped OpenCode command families. Templates, validators, benchmark adapters, and generated routers consume this instead of restating it as prose.\",\n    \"confirm_auto_relationship\": \"The observed 'confirm == auto + checkpoints' relationship holds only for light single-pass mode-pair families (verified on design; inferred for create and speckit:plan). For autonomy-heavy commands (speckit:complete, all deep:*) the :auto workflow carries orchestration machinery the :confirm variant lacks, so the two are divergent siblings and must be modeled independently rather than derived. Downstream checks must not assume the invariant universally.\",\n    \"granularity\": \"One entry per family; router_path is a directory glob for families whose per-operation routers share one uniform pattern (create, design, deep) and an explicit list for families whose routers differ (speckit, memory, doctor).\",\n    \"coverage\": \"Covers the six router-shaped families only. The prompt and rewrite groups and the three root-level utilities (/agent-router, /goal-opencode, /vision) ship no family router and carry no entry here; a consumer that walks this file is walking 31 of the 39 shipped commands, not all of them.\",\n    \"asset_naming\": \"Owned assets are hyphen-joined: <family>-<command>-<kind> for create, speckit, doctor and deep. A family whose commands already read unambiguously drops the family prefix and names assets <command>-<kind> — the memory family (save.md/search.md, now hosted under the speckit command folder as /speckit:save and /speckit:search; save-presentation.txt) and design (extract-auto.yaml) both do. The kind suffixes are -presentation.txt, -auto.yaml and -confirm.yaml. Underscores are not used; the shipped prompt group is the tree's lone underscore holdout and is out of scope here.\",\n    \"path_templates\": \"A per-command asset path carries exactly one <placeholder>, which expands to the router's command name. generate-command-routers.cjs special-cases the memory family key (the internal contract identifier for the save/search direct-dispatch commands) when the placeholder opens the basename; a prefix-dropping family it does not special-case must therefore spell its assets literally rather than as a template, which is why design carries concrete filenames.\"\n  },\n  \"families\": {\n    \"create\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": \".skilled/commands/create/*.md\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<target> [operation] [--path <dir>] [per-command flags] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | omitted\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"confirm\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"$ARGUMENTS resolved in the router's MODE ROUTING section; the foot-of-file `User request: $ARGUMENTS` raw echo is deprecated\",\n        \":auto honors a PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: marker block for non-interactive setup\",\n        \"Stop and report the missing path if any referenced asset is absent\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"writes and overwrites skill and doc files\", \"full-update mutates existing docs\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/create:skill\", \"/create:agent\", \"/create:<operation>\", \":auto suffix\", \":confirm suffix\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"design\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": \".skilled/commands/design/*.md\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<live-url> --output <dir> [--register brand|product] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto | no-suffix with complete args\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | no-suffix with incomplete args\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"conditional-auto\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-confirm.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/references/creation-contract.md (shared lifecycle contract; consumed, owned by sk-design-md-generator)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"--register selects an internal task lane, not an execution mode\",\n        \"Defer to the sk-design hub (STATUS=DEFER ROUTE=hub) when redesign or critique dominates the request\",\n        \"Never auto-chain to a sibling command; next steps are recommend-only\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"writes and overwrites DESIGN.md at the resolved --output destination\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/design:extract\", \":auto suffix\", \":confirm suffix\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"speckit\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": [\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/resume.md\"\n      ],\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<feature-description> [:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended|--unattended] [:with-context] [:with-phases]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml (execution_mode auto)\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":autopilot | :unattended | --unattended\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml (execution_mode autopilot; not aliased to :auto)\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | interactive choice\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml (execution_mode confirm)\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-resume-auto.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | interactive choice\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-resume-confirm.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"ask\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\", \":autopilot\", \":unattended\", \"--unattended\"],\n        \"overrides\": [\n          { \"command\": \"/speckit:resume\", \"default_policy\": \"confirm\" }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>-auto.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>-confirm.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \":auto honors a PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: marker block\",\n        \"Unattended planning writes per-task metadata (agent, deps, touched-files) into tasks.md\",\n        \"Dispatched-agent I/O uses envelopes tagged schema_version agent-io/v1\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": {\n        \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\",\n        \"exceptions\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"/speckit:complete, /speckit:implement\",\n            \"surface\": \"SPECKIT_AUTOPILOT_RESULT machine result line and fixed reason codes\",\n            \"reason\": \"Router-owned machine status grammar for unattended runs, not a visible presentation block\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"implement and complete mutate repository code\", \"run validation gates\", \"autopilot merges git branches after clean verification\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\", \"/speckit:resume\", \":auto suffix\", \":confirm suffix\", \":autopilot suffix\", \":unattended suffix\", \"--unattended flag\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/agent-io-contract.md\"\n    },\n    \"continuity\": {\n      \"topology\": \"direct-dispatch\",\n      \"router_path\": [\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/save.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\"\n      ],\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": false,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"per-command: save <spec-folder>; search <query> [--packet <specFolder>] [--triggers] [--paths] [--count]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \"save\", \"target\": \"generate-context.js continuity-metadata refresh; no index hand-off\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"search\", \"target\": \"lookup-trigger-index.mjs for declared trigger phrases; the ripgrep recipes in retrieval-conventions.md for free text\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"non-mutating-default\",\n        \"supported_modes\": []\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/<command>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"script\", \"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js (consumed; owned by system-spec-kit)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"search runs an embedded bash pre-processing line before policy that emits ARGS_PRESENT and QUERY; the router binds control flow to that output rather than re-deriving argument presence\",\n        \"Never query the database with raw sqlite3 or Bash\",\n        \"memory/learn is a deprecated tombstone: it owns a presentation asset carrying the deprecation wording but binds no execution target, so a mode or workflow check that applies to the live save/search commands does not apply to it\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": {\n        \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\",\n        \"exceptions\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"/speckit:search\",\n            \"surface\": \"Inline five-core-slot SPECKIT:SEARCH render block (search.md render-fidelity reminder)\",\n            \"reason\": \"Sanctioned render-fidelity exception: the presentation asset stays the source of truth; the router inlines only the compressed retrieval shape as a hard render reminder\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": false,\n        \"gated\": false,\n        \"operations\": []\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/speckit:save\", \"/speckit:search\", \"flags on search (e.g. /speckit:search \\\"query\\\" --triggers, --paths, --count)\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"doctor\": {\n      \"topology\": \"subaction-route-manifest\",\n      \"router_path\": [\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/deep-loop.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/runtime-mirrors.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/sk-code.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/git.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/update.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/env.md\"\n      ],\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"per-command: [speckit-retrieval] | list | ? (speckit); <tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ? (skill-advisor); [--scope=research|review|council|both|all] (deep-loop); no arguments (runtime-mirrors); [setup] [--prompt=<text>] (sk-code); <hooks|standards> [--dry-run] | list | ? (git); <install [--runtime <name>]|debug [--fix]> (mcp); [check|align|apply|rollback|record-base|compat] [--release=<tag>] [--scope=all|<unit,...>] [--remote=<name-or-url>] [--dry-run] [flags] (update); [list | <section> | <VARIABLE>] [--dry-run] (env)\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \"<target> resolved via _routes.yaml for speckit, skill-advisor, deep-loop, runtime-mirrors, sk-code and git\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<the route's yaml>, named per route in _routes.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"install | debug\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-mcp-<sub>.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"check\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"align\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-align.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"apply\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-apply.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"rollback\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-rollback.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"record-base\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-record-base.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"compat\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-compat-action.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"list | section | variable [--dry-run]\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"confirm-only\",\n        \"supported_modes\": []\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"route_manifest\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-<entry>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-align.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-apply.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-rollback.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-record-base.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-compat-action.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-<target>.yaml (per-route target workflows, named by each route's yaml field)\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"script\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh (validates _routes.yaml)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset and _routes.yaml before dispatch\",\n        \"Parse the positional target before any flag; reject cross-target flags before loading the target YAML\",\n        \"Bare /doctor:update runs the read-only check action, and /doctor:update apply, rollback, record-base and compat each request approval before their first write\",\n        \"The manifest exposes each route's mutation class (read-only | add-only | mutates) and gate-3 location before acting\",\n        \"Each _routes.yaml route names its owning command; a command that owns one route (speckit, deep-loop, runtime-mirrors, sk-code) takes no required positional, and input.required is true for the skill-advisor, git and mcp routers only\",\n        \"/doctor:speckit answers a target another doctor command owns with a moved-target notice and loads no workflow\",\n        \"/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild backs up skill-graph.sqlite before advisor_rebuild and restores it when the rebuild or its validation fails\",\n        \"/doctor:git hooks writes only git config speckit.hooks.<key> in local or global scope after an approved plan, and refuses the per-push approvals; /doctor:git standards writes only .sk-git/ or the skgit.contractDir directory, never the shipped sk-git templates; /doctor:git setup is read-only and writes nothing\",\n        \"/doctor:env reads ENV-REFERENCE.md at every invocation, reports only secret source presence, and supports list plus section or variable selectors and --dry-run\",\n        \"/doctor:env has no required positional; it writes only an explicitly confirmed eligible preference to hook-flags.env or Claude settings and never writes .env or a shell profile\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"skill-advisor tune writes lib/scorer/lanes sources\", \"skill-advisor rebuild rewrites skill-graph.sqlite through the advisor CLI after a backup\", \"git hooks sets or unsets one speckit.hooks.<key> git config value per approved change\", \"git standards copies the shipped sk-git templates into .sk-git/ and edits those copies per approved change, re-validated before each write\", \"mcp install writes the Code Mode build, selected runtime config and .utcp_config.json; credential values remain operator-managed in root .env\", \"update apply writes only the engine's displayed release plan after one startup approval, records rollback.json before target writes and runs the post-apply battery\", \"update rollback restores a run's rollback record after one approval and clears a stale apply lock only with its own approval\", \"update record-base writes .skilled/release/base.json after one approval\", \"update compat moves .opencode/specs to specs/ after one approval and runs upgrade-legacy --apply after a second approval, logging each move step in the git directory\", \"env updates one eligible preference in hook-flags.env or the Claude settings env block after explicit confirmation\"]\n      },\n      \"routing_source\": \"manifest\",\n      \"timeout_bounds\": { \"warm_probe_timeout_ms\": 500 },\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/doctor:speckit\", \"/doctor:speckit list\", \"/doctor:skill-advisor <target>\", \"/doctor:skill-advisor list\", \"/doctor:deep-loop [--scope=<scope>]\", \"/doctor:runtime-mirrors\", \"/doctor:sk-code [setup] [--prompt=<text>]\", \"/doctor:git <hooks|standards|setup>\", \"/doctor:git list\", \"/doctor:mcp <install|debug>\", \"/doctor:update [check|align|apply|rollback|record-base|compat] [flags]\", \"/doctor:env [list | <section> | <VARIABLE>] [--dry-run]\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"deep\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/*.md\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=<type>] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-auto.yaml (dispatches LEAF iteration agents)\" },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | interactive choice\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"ask\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-confirm.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/ (generated *.contract.md + manifest.jsonl digest ledger)\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/legacy/ (fallback injection bodies)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"One hard-block gate: the BLOCKED unified setup phase (do not load YAML until all required inputs are bound)\",\n        \":auto honors a PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: marker block and persists a config json before loading YAML\",\n        \"Acquire the research/review lock before folder-state classification\",\n        \"--dry-run is a first-class flag on /deep:research's confirm flow, not a third execution mode and not a family-wide flag\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": false,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"add-only artifact writes (reports, iteration state, deltas, logs); routes code changes to speckit rather than mutating directly\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": {\n        \"lineage_timeout_hours_default\": 4,\n        \"executor_timeout\": \"bounded per-invocation by --executor-timeout=SECONDS\"\n      },\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/deep:research\", \"/deep:review\", \"/deep:ai-council\", \"attached suffix (e.g. /deep:research:auto)\", \"--dry-run flag (/deep:research only)\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n---TEMPLATE---\n---\ntitle: Command Template - OpenCode Slash Commands\ndescription: Templates and best practices for creating production-quality slash commands in OpenCode with proper frontmatter and structure.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"slash command template\"\n  - \"command frontmatter structure\"\n  - \"opencode command scaffold\"\n  - \"argument hint patterns\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.0.1.0\n---\n\n# Command Template - OpenCode Slash Commands\n\nTemplates for creating slash commands with proper frontmatter, mandatory gates, and structured workflows.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### What Are OpenCode Commands?\n\n**OpenCode commands** are slash-triggered instructions (e.g., `/speckit:complete`, `/speckit:save`) that automate workflows, enforce patterns, and extend AI agent capabilities. They're markdown files that define structured behavior for specific tasks.\n\n**Core Purpose**:\n- **Workflow automation** - Multi-step processes become single invocations\n- **Pattern enforcement** - Consistent behavior across sessions\n- **Task routing** - Arguments dispatch to appropriate handlers\n- **User guidance** - Structured prompts prevent errors\n- **Tool restriction** - Limit which tools the command can use\n\n**Key Difference from Skills**:\n- Commands = Actionable workflows triggered by `/command-name`\n- Skills = Reference documentation loaded via `Read(\".skilled/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\")`\n\n### Core Characteristics\n\n| Characteristic         | Description                                           |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Markdown-based**     | Human-readable instruction files                      |\n| **Frontmatter-driven** | Metadata controls behavior (description, args, tools) |\n| **Argument-aware**     | Parse and validate user input via `$ARGUMENTS`        |\n| **Status-reporting**   | Return structured outcomes (`STATUS=OK\\|FAIL`)        |\n| **Tool-restricted**    | `allowed-tools` limits available tools                |\n\n### How Commands Are Invoked\n\n```\nUser types: /command-name arguments\n                │           │\n                │           └─► Passed as $ARGUMENTS variable\n                │\n                └─► OpenCode finds .opencode/commands/command-name.md\n                    │\n                    ├─► Loads frontmatter (description, tools, hints)\n                    │\n                    ├─► Injects $ARGUMENTS into instruction body\n                    │\n                    └─► AI agent executes instructions step-by-step\n```\n\n> **Description budget**: command `description:` fields share the Claude Code skill-metadata budget (default 8,000 chars total). Keep each command description **≤ 110 chars**, retain `:auto`/`:confirm` mode suffixes (advisor trigger tokens), no product enumerations. See [`assets/frontmatter-templates.md` § Description Budget & Trim Style](../../sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md) for the canonical trim rules.\n\n### Command File Location\n\n```\n.skilled/\n└── command/\n    ├── simple-command.md          → /simple-command\n    ├── workflow-command.md        → /workflow-command\n    └── namespace/                  → Grouped commands\n        ├── action1.md             → /namespace:action1\n        └── action2.md             → /namespace:action2\n```\n\n### Progressive Complexity\n\n```\nLevel 1: Simple Command\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"./command-contract.schema.json\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"purpose\": \"Single machine-readable source of behavioral truth for the six router-shaped OpenCode command families. Templates, validators, benchmark adapters, and generated routers consume this instead of restating it as prose.\",\n    \"confirm_auto_relationship\": \"The observed 'confirm == auto + checkpoints' relationship holds only for light single-pass mode-pair families (verified on design; inferred for create and speckit:plan). For autonomy-heavy commands (speckit:complete, all deep:*) the :auto workflow carries orchestration machinery the :confirm variant lacks, so the two are divergent siblings and must be modeled independently rather than derived. Downstream checks must not assume the invariant universally.\",\n    \"granularity\": \"One entry per family; router_path is a directory glob for families whose per-operation routers share one uniform pattern (create, design, deep) and an explicit list for families whose routers differ (speckit, memory, doctor).\",\n    \"coverage\": \"Covers the six router-shaped families only. The prompt and rewrite groups and the three root-level utilities (/agent-router, /goal-opencode, /vision) ship no family router and carry no entry here; a consumer that walks this file is walking 31 of the 39 shipped commands, not all of them.\",\n    \"asset_naming\": \"Owned assets are hyphen-joined: <family>-<command>-<kind> for create, speckit, doctor and deep. A family whose commands already read unambiguously drops the family prefix and names assets <command>-<kind> — the memory family (save.md/search.md, now hosted under the speckit command folder as /speckit:save and /speckit:search; save-presentation.txt) and design (extract-auto.yaml) both do. The kind suffixes are -presentation.txt, -auto.yaml and -confirm.yaml. Underscores are not used; the shipped prompt group is the tree's lone underscore holdout and is out of scope here.\",\n    \"path_templates\": \"A per-command asset path carries exactly one <placeholder>, which expands to the router's command name. generate-command-routers.cjs special-cases the memory family key (the internal contract identifier for the save/search direct-dispatch commands) when the placeholder opens the basename; a prefix-dropping family it does not special-case must therefore spell its assets literally rather than as a template, which is why design carries concrete filenames.\"\n  },\n  \"families\": {\n    \"create\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": \".skilled/commands/create/*.md\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<target> [operation] [--path <dir>] [per-command flags] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | omitted\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"confirm\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-<name>-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"$ARGUMENTS resolved in the router's MODE ROUTING section; the foot-of-file `User request: $ARGUMENTS` raw echo is deprecated\",\n        \":auto honors a PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: marker block for non-interactive setup\",\n        \"Stop and report the missing path if any referenced asset is absent\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"writes and overwrites skill and doc files\", \"full-update mutates existing docs\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/create:skill\", \"/create:agent\", \"/create:<operation>\", \":auto suffix\", \":confirm suffix\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"design\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": \".skilled/commands/design/*.md\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<live-url> --output <dir> [--register brand|product] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto | no-suffix with complete args\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | no-suffix with incomplete args\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"conditional-auto\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/design/assets/extract-confirm.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/references/creation-contract.md (shared lifecycle contract; consumed, owned by sk-design-md-generator)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"--register selects an internal task lane, not an execution mode\",\n        \"Defer to the sk-design hub (STATUS=DEFER ROUTE=hub) when redesign or critique dominates the request\",\n        \"Never auto-chain to a sibling command; next steps are recommend-only\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"writes and overwrites DESIGN.md at the resolved --output destination\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/design:extract\", \":auto suffix\", \":confirm suffix\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"speckit\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": [\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/resume.md\"\n      ],\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<feature-description> [:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended|--unattended] [:with-context] [:with-phases]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml (execution_mode auto)\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":autopilot | :unattended | --unattended\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml (execution_mode autopilot; not aliased to :auto)\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | interactive choice\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml (execution_mode confirm)\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-resume-auto.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | interactive choice\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-resume-confirm.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"ask\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\", \":autopilot\", \":unattended\", \"--unattended\"],\n        \"overrides\": [\n          { \"command\": \"/speckit:resume\", \"default_policy\": \"confirm\" }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\"] },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>-auto.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-<name>-confirm.yaml\", \"commands\": [\"/speckit:resume\"] }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \":auto honors a PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: marker block\",\n        \"Unattended planning writes per-task metadata (agent, deps, touched-files) into tasks.md\",\n        \"Dispatched-agent I/O uses envelopes tagged schema_version agent-io/v1\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": {\n        \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\",\n        \"exceptions\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"/speckit:complete, /speckit:implement\",\n            \"surface\": \"SPECKIT_AUTOPILOT_RESULT machine result line and fixed reason codes\",\n            \"reason\": \"Router-owned machine status grammar for unattended runs, not a visible presentation block\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"implement and complete mutate repository code\", \"run validation gates\", \"autopilot merges git branches after clean verification\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/speckit:plan\", \"/speckit:implement\", \"/speckit:complete\", \"/speckit:resume\", \":auto suffix\", \":confirm suffix\", \":autopilot suffix\", \":unattended suffix\", \"--unattended flag\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/agent-io-contract.md\"\n    },\n    \"continuity\": {\n      \"topology\": \"direct-dispatch\",\n      \"router_path\": [\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/save.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\"\n      ],\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": false,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"per-command: save <spec-folder>; search <query> [--packet <specFolder>] [--triggers] [--paths] [--count]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \"save\", \"target\": \"generate-context.js continuity-metadata refresh; no index hand-off\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"search\", \"target\": \"lookup-trigger-index.mjs for declared trigger phrases; the ripgrep recipes in retrieval-conventions.md for free text\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"non-mutating-default\",\n        \"supported_modes\": []\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/<command>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"script\", \"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js (consumed; owned by system-spec-kit)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"search runs an embedded bash pre-processing line before policy that emits ARGS_PRESENT and QUERY; the router binds control flow to that output rather than re-deriving argument presence\",\n        \"Never query the database with raw sqlite3 or Bash\",\n        \"memory/learn is a deprecated tombstone: it owns a presentation asset carrying the deprecation wording but binds no execution target, so a mode or workflow check that applies to the live save/search commands does not apply to it\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": {\n        \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\",\n        \"exceptions\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"/speckit:search\",\n            \"surface\": \"Inline five-core-slot SPECKIT:SEARCH render block (search.md render-fidelity reminder)\",\n            \"reason\": \"Sanctioned render-fidelity exception: the presentation asset stays the source of truth; the router inlines only the compressed retrieval shape as a hard render reminder\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": false,\n        \"gated\": false,\n        \"operations\": []\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": null,\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/speckit:save\", \"/speckit:search\", \"flags on search (e.g. /speckit:search \\\"query\\\" --triggers, --paths, --count)\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"doctor\": {\n      \"topology\": \"subaction-route-manifest\",\n      \"router_path\": [\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/deep-loop.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/runtime-mirrors.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/sk-code.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/git.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/update.md\",\n        \".skilled/commands/doctor/env.md\"\n      ],\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"per-command: [speckit-retrieval] | list | ? (speckit); <tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ? (skill-advisor); [--scope=research|review|council|both|all] (deep-loop); no arguments (runtime-mirrors); [setup] [--prompt=<text>] (sk-code); <hooks|standards> [--dry-run] | list | ? (git); <install [--runtime <name>]|debug [--fix]> (mcp); [check|align|apply|rollback|record-base|compat] [--release=<tag>] [--scope=all|<unit,...>] [--remote=<name-or-url>] [--dry-run] [flags] (update); [list | <section> | <VARIABLE>] [--dry-run] (env)\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \"<target> resolved via _routes.yaml for speckit, skill-advisor, deep-loop, runtime-mirrors, sk-code and git\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<the route's yaml>, named per route in _routes.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"install | debug\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-mcp-<sub>.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"check\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"align\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-align.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"apply\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-apply.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"rollback\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-rollback.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"record-base\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-record-base.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"compat\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-compat-action.yaml\" },\n        { \"selector\": \"list | section | variable [--dry-run]\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"confirm-only\",\n        \"supported_modes\": []\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"route_manifest\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-<entry>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-check.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-align.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-apply.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-rollback.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-record-base.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-compat-action.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-<target>.yaml (per-route target workflows, named by each route's yaml field)\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"script\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh (validates _routes.yaml)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset and _routes.yaml before dispatch\",\n        \"Parse the positional target before any flag; reject cross-target flags before loading the target YAML\",\n        \"Bare /doctor:update runs the read-only check action, and /doctor:update apply, rollback, record-base and compat each request approval before their first write\",\n        \"The manifest exposes each route's mutation class (read-only | add-only | mutates) and gate-3 location before acting\",\n        \"Each _routes.yaml route names its owning command; a command that owns one route (speckit, deep-loop, runtime-mirrors, sk-code) takes no required positional, and input.required is true for the skill-advisor, git and mcp routers only\",\n        \"/doctor:speckit answers a target another doctor command owns with a moved-target notice and loads no workflow\",\n        \"/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild backs up skill-graph.sqlite before advisor_rebuild and restores it when the rebuild or its validation fails\",\n        \"/doctor:git hooks writes only git config speckit.hooks.<key> in local or global scope after an approved plan, and refuses the per-push approvals; /doctor:git standards writes only .sk-git/ or the skgit.contractDir directory, never the shipped sk-git templates; /doctor:git setup is read-only and writes nothing\",\n        \"/doctor:env reads ENV-REFERENCE.md at every invocation, reports only secret source presence, and supports list plus section or variable selectors and --dry-run\",\n        \"/doctor:env has no required positional; it writes only an explicitly confirmed eligible preference to hook-flags.env or Claude settings and never writes .env or a shell profile\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": true,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"skill-advisor tune writes lib/scorer/lanes sources\", \"skill-advisor rebuild rewrites skill-graph.sqlite through the advisor CLI after a backup\", \"git hooks sets or unsets one speckit.hooks.<key> git config value per approved change\", \"git standards copies the shipped sk-git templates into .sk-git/ and edits those copies per approved change, re-validated before each write\", \"mcp install writes the Code Mode build, selected runtime config and .utcp_config.json; credential values remain operator-managed in root .env\", \"update apply writes only the engine's displayed release plan after one startup approval, records rollback.json before target writes and runs the post-apply battery\", \"update rollback restores a run's rollback record after one approval and clears a stale apply lock only with its own approval\", \"update record-base writes .skilled/release/base.json after one approval\", \"update compat moves .opencode/specs to specs/ after one approval and runs upgrade-legacy --apply after a second approval, logging each move step in the git directory\", \"env updates one eligible preference in hook-flags.env or the Claude settings env block after explicit confirmation\"]\n      },\n      \"routing_source\": \"manifest\",\n      \"timeout_bounds\": { \"warm_probe_timeout_ms\": 500 },\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/doctor:speckit\", \"/doctor:speckit list\", \"/doctor:skill-advisor <target>\", \"/doctor:skill-advisor list\", \"/doctor:deep-loop [--scope=<scope>]\", \"/doctor:runtime-mirrors\", \"/doctor:sk-code [setup] [--prompt=<text>]\", \"/doctor:git <hooks|standards|setup>\", \"/doctor:git list\", \"/doctor:mcp <install|debug>\", \"/doctor:update [check|align|apply|rollback|record-base|compat] [flags]\", \"/doctor:env [list | <section> | <VARIABLE>] [--dry-run]\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": null\n    },\n    \"deep\": {\n      \"topology\": \"mode-pair\",\n      \"router_path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/*.md\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"gate_owner\": \"router\",\n        \"argument_hint\": \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=<type>] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\n      },\n      \"execution_targets\": [\n        { \"selector\": \":auto\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-auto.yaml (dispatches LEAF iteration agents)\" },\n        { \"selector\": \":confirm | interactive choice\", \"target\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-confirm.yaml\" }\n      ],\n      \"mode_matrix\": {\n        \"default_policy\": \"ask\",\n        \"supported_modes\": [\":auto\", \":confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"owned_assets\": [\n        { \"purpose\": \"presentation\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-presentation.txt\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"auto_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-auto.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"confirm_workflow\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-<name>-confirm.yaml\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/ (generated *.contract.md + manifest.jsonl digest ledger)\" },\n        { \"purpose\": \"other\", \"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/legacy/ (fallback injection bodies)\" }\n      ],\n      \"loader_requirements\": [\n        \"Read the presentation asset before showing any startup question\",\n        \"One hard-block gate: the BLOCKED unified setup phase (do not load YAML until all required inputs are bound)\",\n        \":auto honors a PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: marker block and persists a config json before loading YAML\",\n        \"Acquire the research/review lock before folder-state classification\",\n        \"--dry-run is a first-class flag on /deep:research's confirm flow, not a third execution mode and not a family-wide flag\"\n      ],\n      \"presentation\": { \"owner\": \"presentation-asset\", \"exceptions\": [] },\n      \"destructive_policy\": {\n        \"has_destructive_ops\": false,\n        \"gated\": true,\n        \"operations\": [\"add-only artifact writes (reports, iteration state, deltas, logs); routes code changes to speckit rather than mutating directly\"]\n      },\n      \"timeout_bounds\": {\n        \"lineage_timeout_hours_default\": 4,\n        \"executor_timeout\": \"bounded per-invocation by --executor-timeout=SECONDS\"\n      },\n      \"invocation_aliases\": [\"/deep:research\", \"/deep:review\", \"/deep:ai-council\", \"attached suffix (e.g. /deep:research:auto)\", \"--dry-run flag (/deep:research only)\"],\n      \"workflow_schema_ref\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n---TEMPLATE---\n---\ntitle: Command Template - OpenCode Slash Commands\ndescription: Templates and best practices for creating production-quality slash commands in OpenCode with proper frontmatter and structure.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"slash command template\"\n  - \"command frontmatter structure\"\n  - \"opencode command scaffold\"\n  - \"argument hint patterns\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.0.1.0\n---\n\n# Command Template - OpenCode Slash Commands\n\nTemplates for creating slash commands with proper frontmatter, mandatory gates, and structured workflows.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### What Are OpenCode Commands?\n\n**OpenCode commands** are slash-triggered instructions (e.g., `/speckit:complete`, `/speckit:save`) that automate workflows, enforce patterns, and extend AI agent capabilities. They're markdown files that define structured behavior for specific tasks.\n\n**Core Purpose**:\n- **Workflow automation** - Multi-step processes become single invocations\n- **Pattern enforcement** - Consistent behavior across sessions\n- **Task routing** - Arguments dispatch to appropriate handlers\n- **User guidance** - Structured prompts prevent errors\n- **Tool restriction** - Limit which tools the command can use\n\n**Key Difference from Skills**:\n- Commands = Actionable workflows triggered by `/command-name`\n- Skills = Reference documentation loaded via `Read(\".skilled/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\")`\n\n### Core Characteristics\n\n| Characteristic         | Description                                           |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Markdown-based**     | Human-readable instruction files                      |\n| **Frontmatter-driven** | Metadata controls behavior (description, args, tools) |\n| **Argument-aware**     | Parse and validate user input via `$ARGUMENTS`        |\n| **Status-reporting**   | Return structured outcomes (`STATUS=OK\\|FAIL`)        |\n| **Tool-restricted**    | `allowed-tools` limits available tools                |\n\n### How Commands Are Invoked\n\n```\nUser types: /command-name arguments\n                │           │\n                │           └─► Passed as $ARGUMENTS variable\n                │\n                └─► OpenCode finds .opencode/commands/command-name.md\n                    │\n                    ├─► Loads frontmatter (description, tools, hints)\n                    │\n                    ├─► Injects $ARGUMENTS into instruction body\n                    │\n                    └─► AI agent executes instructions step-by-step\n```\n\n> **Description budget**: command `description:` fields share the Claude Code skill-metadata budget (default 8,000 chars total). Keep each command description **≤ 110 chars**, retain `:auto`/`:confirm` mode suffixes (advisor trigger tokens), no product enumerations. See [`assets/frontmatter-templates.md` § Description Budget & Trim Style](../../sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-templates.md) for the canonical trim rules.\n\n### Command File Location\n\n```\n.skilled/\n└── command/\n    ├── simple-command.md          → /simple-command\n    ├── workflow-command.md        → /workflow-command\n    └── namespace/                  → Grouped commands\n        ├── action1.md             → /namespace:action1\n        └── action2.md             → /namespace:action2\n```\n\n### Progressive Complexity\n\n```\nLevel 1: Simple Command\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-contract.json; echo \"---TEMPLATE---\"; sed -n 1,80p .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md","time":{"start":1792430567695,"end":1792430567712}},"id":"prt_1552ff04f0015Jd1c1516IE26e","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552fe1b2001lLgEvPtp6w2PWx"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430568030,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_PcvUKYKsNqSfJYSTDNAl9151","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"allowed-tools\\|argument-hint\\|description\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md | head -20; echo \"---VALIDATOR---\"; find .skilled/skills/sk-doc -iname \"*command*valid*\" -o -iname \"*validate*command*\" | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:3:description: Choose command vs skill vs agent before drafting, then avoid the recurring command-authoring mistakes - missing gates, over-broad tools, dashboards in routers, and multiline descriptions.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:9:  - \"command allowed-tools mistake\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:23:This reference guards two failure modes: choosing the wrong component (a command when a skill or agent fits better) and the recurring command-authoring defects: missing gates, over-broad tools, dashboards in routers, and multiline descriptions. Decide the component first, then check the draft against the mistakes table.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:54:| Omitting `argument-hint` for required input | Users cannot see what the invocation expects | Add a precise hint with `<required>` and `[optional]` parts |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:59:| Over-broad `allowed-tools` | The command can use tools outside its contract | Reduce the list to the tools actually required |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:60:| Using bare MCP names in `allowed-tools` | Runtime tool resolution can drift from the configured namespace | Use fully qualified `mcp__<server>__<tool>` IDs |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:61:| Writing a multi-line description | Help output and metadata consumers expect a single-line summary | Keep `description` one line and move detail into the body |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:70:- [argument-hints-and-modes.md](argument-hints-and-modes.md) - correct hint, mode, and frontmatter patterns\n---VALIDATOR---\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:3:description: Choose command vs skill vs agent before drafting, then avoid the recurring command-authoring mistakes - missing gates, over-broad tools, dashboards in routers, and multiline descriptions.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:9:  - \"command allowed-tools mistake\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:23:This reference guards two failure modes: choosing the wrong component (a command when a skill or agent fits better) and the recurring command-authoring defects: missing gates, over-broad tools, dashboards in routers, and multiline descriptions. Decide the component first, then check the draft against the mistakes table.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:54:| Omitting `argument-hint` for required input | Users cannot see what the invocation expects | Add a precise hint with `<required>` and `[optional]` parts |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:59:| Over-broad `allowed-tools` | The command can use tools outside its contract | Reduce the list to the tools actually required |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:60:| Using bare MCP names in `allowed-tools` | Runtime tool resolution can drift from the configured namespace | Use fully qualified `mcp__<server>__<tool>` IDs |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:61:| Writing a multi-line description | Help output and metadata consumers expect a single-line summary | Keep `description` one line and move detail into the body |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md:70:- [argument-hints-and-modes.md](argument-hints-and-modes.md) - correct hint, mode, and frontmatter patterns\n---VALIDATOR---\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"allowed-tools\\|argument-hint\\|description\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/references/common-pitfalls.md | head -20; echo \"---VALIDATOR---\"; find .skilled/skills/sk-doc -iname \"*command*valid*\" -o -iname \"*validate*command*\" | head -10","time":{"start":1792430567979,"end":1792430568029}},"id":"prt_1552ff11e0010Bc3Wp1pkUOGuw","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_1552fe1b2001lLgEvPtp6w2PWx"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1792430569158,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"id":"prt_1552ff6c4001ICsmcGeC9tz2P6","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"7878b1478f09f67aa979fd58fdedbc0a4b78607c","messageID":"msg_1552fe1b2001lLgEvPtp6w2PWx","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":232708,"input":2195,"output":205,"reasoning":36,"cache":{"write":0,"read":230272}},"cost":0.0010481994}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792430572990,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"id":"prt_1553005bc001OORRCtHI8CQYWY","messageID":"msg_1552ffb2f001scLFnhykTD92ir","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","snapshot":"7878b1478f09f67aa979fd58fdedbc0a4b78607c","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430578987,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_6rcjOmSkAwwNlY9dcMOh3225","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"Stop event\\|pending |\\|armed |\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md | head -10; echo \"---CATALOG---\"; sed -n 1,80p .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/context-preservation/session-relaunch-loop.md"},"output":"29:Codex binds three repo hooks rendered from `hook-registry.json` into [.codex/hooks.json](../../../.codex/hooks.json). `prompt-seed.mjs` binds `UserPromptSubmit`: a `[session-relaunch]` prompt receives the claim-seed instructions, and a non-seed prompt runs the same threshold check as `context-nudge.mjs`, which binds `PostToolUse`. The Codex hook installer allows each script under one event only, so seed detection and the mid-session nudge are separate entry points over `shared.mjs`. The fill comes from the transcript rollout's latest `token_count` event: `last_token_usage.input_tokens` is the numerator and `cached_input_tokens` stays out because it is already inside that count. The window is `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, then the event's `model_context_window`. The nudge reaches the model as `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, the envelope the repo's other Codex adapters emit. `stop-arm.mjs` accepts only payloads whose `hook_event_name` is `Stop`. It resolves the target, arms a matching pending record, then spawns the killer with `--transcript <transcript_path>`. A spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next Stop restarts its killer. Codex exports no pid variable, so the killer target resolves through the same ancestor rule the CLI's running-work check uses. `skilled-loop codex` always starts Codex with `--no-daemon` because its shared app-server daemon keeps the environment of the session that started it. In a git worktree, Codex reads its `hooks.json` from the main checkout, not the worktree. The automatic hop needs the session-relaunch rows in the main checkout's file. Each of those three rows, like the three session-relaunch rows in the Claude settings file, carries the repo's hook-drift fallback: a missing adapter prints a `mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<script>` line on stderr and still returns an envelope the host accepts. Claude's fallback adds `mkHookDrift: true`. Codex omits that key, because it rejects unknown keys, and answers its Stop event with `systemMessage` instead of `hookSpecificOutput`, because it rejects that envelope on Stop.\n127:| pending | Prepare accepted the note. Stop has not armed the record yet. |\n128:| armed | A matching Stop event found no remaining background tasks and started the killer. |\n129:| disarmed | The killer ended the record without a relaunch. A session that never went idle before the deadline, a transcript unreadable for 1 s and a session still running after the SIGTERM grace period end with reason `killer-timeout`. A record whose hop count already reached `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS` ends with reason `hop-cap`, and the killer sends no signal. |\n---CATALOG---\n---\ntitle: \"Session relaunch loop\"\ndescription: \"Hands a session near its context limit to a fresh one through a structured handoff note and the skilled-loop wrapper.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"Session relaunch loop\"\n  - \"Claude session relaunch\"\n  - \"Pi session relaunch\"\n  - \"OpenCode session relaunch\"\n  - \"Codex session relaunch\"\n  - \"Hermes session relaunch\"\n  - \"Cursor session relaunch\"\n  - \"Devin session relaunch\"\n  - \"/speckit:handoff session relaunch\"\n  - \"skilled-loop claude\"\n  - \"skilled-loop pi\"\n  - \"skilled-loop opencode\"\n  - \"skilled-loop codex\"\n  - \"skilled-loop hermes\"\n  - \"context handoff to a fresh session\"\nversion: 1.0.2.0\n---\n\n# Session relaunch loop (skilled-loop)\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nShares a structured context handoff across seven runtimes through adapter nudges, a validated note and a wrapper relaunch. Claude Code, Pi, OpenCode, Codex and Hermes run automatically through their adapters. Cursor and Devin run on the `/speckit:handoff` command trigger only.\n\nAn automatic adapter asks for a note near its context threshold, validates and prepares it, then arms it at its host's turn-end event. The skilled-loop wrapper starts the selected runtime with a claim seed when the record is armed, fresh and below the hop cap.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Nudge, Prepare And Arm\n\nClaude's context-nudge handles PostToolUse and UserPromptSubmit. It reads the latest main-chain assistant usage and compares it with the configured threshold. The default is 0.80. One additional nudge fires 0.05 above that level. Each level fires once. The text opens with the measured fill as `Context is about N% full`. Once the ratio passes 1 it names the overflow as `past the configured window (over 100% full)` instead, so an over-wide window reads as overflow rather than as a percentage above 100. It then offers the shortcut before the steps: `If the remaining work fits in a few more steps, finish it instead and skip these steps.` Otherwise the handoff steps come first, before any other work. It accepts session ids matching [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}. Transcript read errors produce no usage. Failed Claude settings reads are treated as absent while the resolver checks its next source or model default. If the operator says not to hand off, the nudge yields and the session keeps working. Auto-compaction remains the fallback.\n\nEvery adapter asks the same questions before it nudges. A pending record for this session silences the nudge. So does an armed one, until it passes its age limit, because the handoff work is already done. The limit is `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_AGE_MIN`, read from the hook config file and then the environment, as the wrapper reads it. Past that limit the wrapper would decline the record as stale, so the nudge resumes instead of waiting on a relaunch that cannot happen. At the hop cap no adapter nudges, because a prepare there can only decline. A re-nudge also keeps the note path the session already has open: the shared planner returns that session's existing `status: open` note and only otherwise builds a timestamped path.\n\nBoth `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` instead. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check only. Runtimes without a session-id variable generate an id with `uuidgen` and reuse it for the session.\n\nPrepare validates the note before checking whether the caller runs under skilled-loop. The nudge passes `--runtime <name>`, which must name one of the seven runtimes. Outside the loop, that value overrides the environment or Claude default and the CLI prints the selected runtime's manual claim command before exiting 3. Inside the loop, a supplied runtime must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. A live child of the runtime process also exits 2 when its command name is one of `sh`, `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `dash`, `ksh`, `mksh`, `tcsh`, `csh`, `nu` or `pwsh`, with a leading `-` stripped so a login shell still matches. Any other child program is not detected. A successful prepare below the hop cap writes a pending record and exits 0. At the cap it writes no record: it prints a `hop limit reached` line that names auto-compaction as the fallback, then the manual claim command, logs `prepare-declined` with reason `hop-cap` and exits 3, leaving the note open for the operator's own claim. When a hop goes ahead, prepare marks each note already claimed by this session as `done`, adds `completed_at` and sets `superseded_by` to the new note's basename.\n\nThe note's Remaining work lists only unfinished task work. Note creation, continuity saving and prepare stay outside that section. Claude saves a bound packet with `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin --full-auto <spec-folder>`. Turn-end arming matches the event session id to the prepared record. Missing required payload data or background work leaves it pending. Otherwise, the adapter writes `status: armed` before starting the detached killer. A killer spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next arm event restarts its killer. Every arm path restarts a killer for an armed record with no live killer owner. It does nothing while one is alive.\n\n### Killer And Wrapper\n\nThe killer polls transcript modification time every 100 ms. Once the transcript is idle, it confirms that the target descends from the loop and re-reads the record. It sends SIGTERM only when the record is armed. Before a signal it re-checks the hop cap: a record at the cap is un-armed with reason `hop-cap`, logged as `killer-hop-cap` and left unsignalled with no notification, because no relaunch would follow and the manual claim is already the session's own instruction. Without a transcript it treats elapsed idle time since start as the idle signal. In OpenCode's Bun-hosted plugin, the detached killer runs with node because process.execPath points to the OpenCode CLI. A single failed transcript read does not end supervision. The killer gives up only after the transcript has stayed unreadable for 1 s without a break. That give-up re-reads the record first. When a later prepare armed a different note, it leaves that record alone and logs `killer-timeout-superseded` with the `watched` and `current` note paths. Otherwise it un-arms the record with reason killer-timeout and attempts the notification. Taking over a stale killer lock goes through a takeover mutex that records its owner pid. The mutex is reclaimed when that owner is dead. It is also reclaimed once it has outlived the longest hold a real holder needs. A mutex with no owner file is reclaimed once it is older than 30 s.\n\nSESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS and SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_AGE_MIN both accept zero. Zero max hops declines every relaunch with reason `hop-cap`. Zero max age declines an armed record once its age is greater than zero. The hooks, wrapper and killer append events to relaunch.log with fsync at mode 0600. A new event starts on its own line after a partial last line, so concurrent writers keep one event per line. A corrupt relaunch file is logged and treated as absent, so should-relaunch declines with reason no-file. The command also treats EACCES, ENOTDIR or EISDIR while reading the record as absent. Other command errors exit 2. Context transcript and settings read errors return absent values instead of escaping as exceptions.\n\nskilled-loop defaults to Claude when it receives no arguments or a prompt without a runtime name. The `cursor` arm launches the `cursor-agent` binary. It preserves the first launch arguments, including name flags. It scans name options only until --. Across hops, it carries model selection for all runtimes, the provider for Pi and Hermes, and Pi extension-selection flags. The wrapper applies the same value check to model, name, Pi extension and Pi or Hermes provider options. It leaves a value equal to `--` or starting with `-` in the first launch's arguments and does not carry it into later hops. Relative Pi extension paths are resolved against the wrapper's starting directory. Claude and Pi are the only runtimes with a launch-time name flag.\n\nA matching armed record is consumed only when it is fresh and below the hop cap. `spec_folder` carries three states: a repo-relative packet path, `none` when Gate 3 was answered D) Skip or empty when Gate 3 was never answered. The wrapper adds the path or `none` to the claim seed. The receiver resumes a packet path, skips Gate 3 for `none` and asks Gate 3 when the field is empty. The seed also carries the note path, so every adapter's claim instructions name the real file rather than leaving the `<handoff-path>` placeholder. Seeds printed by earlier builds spell the Skip suffix differently. The receiver still reads them as Skip. AGENTS.md states that a relaunch hop is the same session. The receiving runtime claims the note and continues only its task work. It never runs prepare on an already claimed note.\n\n`SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD` controls when each session is nudged. Keep it well above a fresh session's startup fill plus its remaining work. Codex live runs chained hop after hop at `0.12` because each fresh session reached about 10% on startup alone. `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS` caps completed relaunches. At the cap the chain ends on its own: prepare writes no record, the adapters stop nudging and the killer un-arms an armed record, so a re-nudged receiver is never killed for a relaunch that cannot start. Use a low hop cap for live checks.\n\n### Pi And OpenCode Adapters\n\nPi checks usage at message_end and holds the nudge text there rather than sending it, because the message that crosses the threshold usually carries the prepare call itself. agent_end re-checks the record and the hop cap, then delivers the held text with deliverAs: 'followUp', triggerTurn: true, so the nudge starts its own turn and needs no operator input. It captures a matching seed in before_agent_start and arms the Pi record on agent_end. Its killer-path resolver walks up from the current directory, so it can find killer.cjs from a repository subdirectory. tsconfig.pi.json includes the Pi extension entry for type-checking.\n\nOpenCode reads message.updated and message.part.updated. It pushes the active nudge on every request while this session has no handoff. Outside skilled-loop it keeps pushing until the handoff note exists. A matching claim seed stays in the system prompt on every request of the session until the note leaves the open state or a new non-seed user message arrives, because an auxiliary request can consume the first prompt. The seed enters through experimental.chat.system.transform. The relaunch record is armed on session.idle.\n\nThe wrapper's Pi relaunch carries provider and model selection together with -ne and each -e extension selection from the initial launch. In this repository, start Pi with -ne -e .pi/extensions/session-relaunch.ts because two installed extensions both register --fast. OpenCode is started with -m <provider/model>. The wrapper preserves that model selection across hops.\n\nIn the recorded live runs, OpenCode reported about 1M context tokens for openai/gpt-6-luna and Pi reported 272K. These reported window sizes differ by runtime.\n\n### Codex Adapter\n\nCodex binds three repo hooks rendered from hook-registry.json into .codex/hooks.json, one script per event because the Codex hook installer allows each script under one event only. `prompt-seed.mjs` on UserPromptSubmit returns claim-seed instructions for a `[session-relaunch]` prompt and runs the threshold check for any other prompt. `context-nudge.mjs` on PostToolUse runs the same check mid-session. `stop-arm.mjs` accepts only `hook_event_name: Stop`. It arms a matching pending record before spawning the killer with `--transcript <transcript_path>`, so a spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next Stop restarts its killer.\n\nThe fill reads the rollout's latest `token_count` event at `transcript_path`. The numerator is `last_token_usage.input_tokens`, which already contains the cached share, so `cached_input_tokens` is not added. The window is `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, then the event's `model_context_window`. The nudge reaches the model as `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. Codex exports no pid variable, so the killer target resolves through the ancestor rule the CLI's running-work check uses.\n\n### Hermes Adapter\n\nHermes runs through the enabled `repo-guards` project plugin, which bridges its plugin hooks to the Node entry points under `hermes/`. `post_api_request` records each call's `usage` per session. `pre_llm_call` returns the context adapter's seed text on a `[session-relaunch]` first turn or the handoff text once the fill crosses the threshold, appended to the turn's user message. `on_session_end` accepts a missing event name from the plugin bridge and rejects a supplied name other than `on_session_end`. It arms a pending record for this session before detaching the killer with the Hermes process resolved by the ancestor rule, so a spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next session end restarts its killer.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"29:Codex binds three repo hooks rendered from `hook-registry.json` into [.codex/hooks.json](../../../.codex/hooks.json). `prompt-seed.mjs` binds `UserPromptSubmit`: a `[session-relaunch]` prompt receives the claim-seed instructions, and a non-seed prompt runs the same threshold check as `context-nudge.mjs`, which binds `PostToolUse`. The Codex hook installer allows each script under one event only, so seed detection and the mid-session nudge are separate entry points over `shared.mjs`. The fill comes from the transcript rollout's latest `token_count` event: `last_token_usage.input_tokens` is the numerator and `cached_input_tokens` stays out because it is already inside that count. The window is `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, then the event's `model_context_window`. The nudge reaches the model as `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, the envelope the repo's other Codex adapters emit. `stop-arm.mjs` accepts only payloads whose `hook_event_name` is `Stop`. It resolves the target, arms a matching pending record, then spawns the killer with `--transcript <transcript_path>`. A spawn failure leaves the record armed until the next Stop restarts its killer. Codex exports no pid variable, so the killer target resolves through the same ancestor rule the CLI's running-work check uses. `skilled-loop codex` always starts Codex with `--no-daemon` because its shared app-server daemon keeps the environment of the session that started it. In a git worktree, Codex reads its `hooks.json` from the main checkout, not the worktree. The automatic hop needs the session-relaunch rows in the main checkout's file. Each of those three rows, like the three session-relaunch rows in the Claude settings file, carries the repo's hook-drift fallback: a missing adapter prints a `mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<script>` line on stderr and still returns an envelope the host accepts. Claude's fallback adds `mkHookDrift: true`. Codex omits that key, because it rejects unknown keys, and answers its Stop event with `systemMessage` instead of `hookSpecificOutput`, because it rejects that envelope on Stop.\n127:| pending | Prepare accepted the note. Stop has not armed the record yet. |\n128:| armed | A matching Stop event found no remaining background tasks and started the killer. |\n129:| disarmed | The killer ended the record without a relaunch. A session that never went idle before the deadline, a transcript unreadable for 1 s and a session still running after the SIGTERM grace period end with reason `killer-timeout`. A record whose hop count already reached `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS` ends with reason `hop-cap`, and the killer sends no signal. |\n---CATALOG---\n---\ntitle: \"Session relaunch loop\"\ndescription: \"Hands a session near its context limit to a fresh one through a structured handoff note and the skilled-loop wrapper.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"Session relaunch loop\"\n  - \"Claude session relaunch\"\n  - \"Pi session relaunch\"\n  - \"OpenCode session relaunch\"\n  - \"Codex session relaunch\"\n  - \"Hermes session relaunch\"\n  - \"Cursor session relaunch\"\n  - \"Devin session relaunch\"\n  - \"/speckit:handoff session relaunch\"\n  - \"skilled-loop claude\"\n  - \"skilled-loop pi\"\n  - \"skilled-loop opencode\"\n  - \"skilled-loop codex\"\n  - \"skilled-loop hermes\"\n  - \"context handoff to a fresh session\"\nversion: 1.0.2.0\n---\n\n# Session relaunch loop (skilled-loop)\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nShares a structured context handoff across seven runtim