{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430592310,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_GpKMg7uKtXEnjRIMzRzH2840","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"CLAUDE_PID supplies\\|shell-child check only\\|CLAUDE_PID\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/context-preservation/session-relaunch-loop.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md"},"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:25:`skilled-loop` exports `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` with the selected runtime. It carries the first launch's model for every runtime. Pi and Hermes also carry their provider. Claude and Pi carry their name. Pi carries its extension flags. Relative Pi extension paths resolve against the wrapper's starting directory. `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can omit it and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. Other runtimes pass the id directly. Runtimes with no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse the value. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies Claude's process id only for the shell-child check. `complete` requires only the note path.\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:81:Prepare validates the note first. An invalid note exits 2. Outside `skilled-loop`, it prints a manual claim command and exits 3 without checking for running shell children. Inside the loop, a live child of the runtime process exits 2 when its command name is `sh`, `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `dash`, `ksh`, `mksh`, `tcsh`, `csh`, `nu` or `pwsh`. A leading `-` is stripped before that lookup, so a login shell still matches. Any other child program is not detected. The runtime pid comes from `CLAUDE_PID` when the variable is set. On runtimes without it, the check resolves the runtime as the direct child of the loop on prepare's ancestor chain. When no runtime resolves, it logs `running-work-check-skipped` and skips. A shell that is prepare's own ancestor does not count. `--runtime` must name one of Claude, Pi, OpenCode, Codex, Cursor, Hermes or Devin. Outside `skilled-loop` it overrides the environment or Claude default. Inside the loop, a supplied value must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. The nudge includes the selected runtime in its prepare command. A successful prepare writes a pending record and exits 0. At the hop cap it writes no record, prints the hop-limit line with the manual claim command and exits 3.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/context-preservation/session-relaunch-loop.md:43:Both `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` instead. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check only. Runtimes without a session-id variable generate an id with `uuidgen` and reuse it for the session.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:21:**Inputs:** nothing through `$ARGUMENTS`. Both `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude Code can omit it and use `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. On Claude, `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check. Other runtimes must pass the session id. If a runtime has no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse that id for the session. `spec_folder` records the Gate 3 answer: the repo-relative packet path, `none` after D) Skip or empty when Gate 3 was never answered.\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:25:`skilled-loop` exports `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` with the selected runtime. It carries the first launch's model for every runtime. Pi and Hermes also carry their provider. Claude and Pi carry their name. Pi carries its extension flags. Relative Pi extension paths resolve against the wrapper's starting directory. `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can omit it and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. Other runtimes pass the id directly. Runtimes with no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse the value. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies Claude's process id only for the shell-child check. `complete` requires only the note path.\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md:81:Prepare validates the note first. An invalid note exits 2. Outside `skilled-loop`, it prints a manual claim command and exits 3 without checking for running shell children. Inside the loop, a live child of the runtime process exits 2 when its command name is `sh`, `bash`, `zsh`, `fish`, `dash`, `ksh`, `mksh`, `tcsh`, `csh`, `nu` or `pwsh`. A leading `-` is stripped before that lookup, so a login shell still matches. Any other child program is not detected. The runtime pid comes from `CLAUDE_PID` when the variable is set. On runtimes without it, the check resolves the runtime as the direct child of the loop on prepare's ancestor chain. When no runtime resolves, it logs `running-work-check-skipped` and skips. A shell that is prepare's own ancestor does not count. `--runtime` must name one of Claude, Pi, OpenCode, Codex, Cursor, Hermes or Devin. Outside `skilled-loop` it overrides the environment or Claude default. Inside the loop, a supplied value must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. The nudge includes the selected runtime in its prepare command. A successful prepare writes a pending record and exits 0. At the hop cap it writes no record, prints the hop-limit line with the manual claim command and exits 3.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/context-preservation/session-relaunch-loop.md:43:Both `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude can use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` instead. `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check only. Runtimes without a session-id variable generate an id with `uuidgen` and reuse it for the session.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:21:**Inputs:** nothing through `$ARGUMENTS`. Both `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude Code can omit it and use `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. On Claude, `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check. Other runtimes must pass the session id. If a runtime has no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse that id for the session. `spec_folder` records the Gate 3 answer: the repo-relative packet path, `none` after D) Skip or empty when Gate 3 was never answered.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"CLAUDE_PID supplies\\|shell-child check only\\|CLAUDE_PID\" .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/context-preservation/session-relaunch-loop.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md","time":{"start":1792430592183,"end":1792430592291}},"id":"prt_155304f50001jTZ8PhjgndwQuZ","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_155302816001SETR55hqHooY6K"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430592591,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_PjLjLF9cRVSUz7gsfonC8423","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"save continuity before\\|Save the bound packet\\|save its continuity\\|Write the handoff note\" .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs | head -20"},"output":".skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:2:description: \"Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop: the manual trigger on every runtime.\"\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:27:- When a spec packet is bound: save continuity before the note is written. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to the continuity writer.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:59:### Step 2: Save the bound packet\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:61:When `spec_folder` is a packet path, save its continuity before writing the note so the receiving session's `/speckit:resume` lands on fresh state. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin --full-auto <spec-folder>`. Record the repo-relative packet path in `spec_folder`. When Gate 3 was answered D) Skip, set `spec_folder` to `none` and skip the save. When Gate 3 was never answered, leave `spec_folder` empty.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:63:### Step 3: Write the handoff note\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs:87:    `1. Write the handoff note at ${shellQuote(pathValue)} in exactly this shape:`,\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs:112:      : 'save its continuity first: pipe the save JSON to '\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:2:description: \"Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop: the manual trigger on every runtime.\"\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:27:- When a spec packet is bound: save continuity before the note is written. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to the continuity writer.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:59:### Step 2: Save the bound packet\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:61:When `spec_folder` is a packet path, save its continuity before writing the note so the receiving session's `/speckit:resume` lands on fresh state. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin --full-auto <spec-folder>`. Record the repo-relative packet path in `spec_folder`. When Gate 3 was answered D) Skip, set `spec_folder` to `none` and skip the save. When Gate 3 was never answered, leave `spec_folder` empty.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:63:### Step 3: Write the handoff note\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs:87:    `1. Write the handoff note at ${shellQuote(pathValue)} in exactly this shape:`,\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs:112:      : 'save its continuity first: pipe the save JSON to '\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"save continuity before\\|Save the bound packet\\|save its continuity\\|Write the handoff note\" .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs | head -20","time":{"start":1792430592468,"end":1792430592553}},"id":"prt_1553050da0017X6NCtNczIfjP6","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_155302816001SETR55hqHooY6K"}}
