{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430668510,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_phch2EotOHUVyfleyNnE0009","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"Gate 3\\|spec_folder\\|no answer\\|answered\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"A session with no Gate 3 answer can now hand off near the context limit without an operator prompt. The spec gate exempts the gitignored handoff note, AGENTS.md says so in its gate sentences, and the repo OpenCode default model is pinned. Live run 10 proved the hop on Claude, Pi and OpenCode with zero operator prompts.\"\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:23:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:49:A session that has no Gate 3 answer can now hand off near its context limit and finish the work in a fresh session, with no operator prompt. Before this phase, two framework rules and one hook rule stopped the hop. The spec gate denied the write of the handoff note when enforcement was on and a gate was open. Gate 3 asked the operator before a read-only session wrote its note. The Gate 2 artifact trigger sent the note to sk-doc, which answered `clarify`.\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:53:The spec gate now treats a write under `.skilled/skills/.state/` as gitignored runtime state and lets it through. The one exception is a concern's tracked `README.md` directly under that folder, which stays gated, as does a `.state` folder nested under another path. The two AGENTS.md sentences that decide whether a turn is spec work now say the same thing, so a session reads the exemption before it decides to ask Gate 3 or to route the note to sk-doc.\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:63:| `AGENTS.md` | Modified | Gate 2 artifact trigger (line 70) and Gate 3 \"does not fire\" clause (line 75) name gitignored runtime state |\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:83:Live run 10 came last. Three loops ran in detached tmux sessions through `clean-tmux.sh`, with the Claude session variables and `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset. Each prompt carried no Gate 3 answer, and the thresholds were `SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD=0.05`, `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS=100` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS=1`. Each loop prepared, took SIGTERM, relaunched and declined a further hop. Nothing was committed, pushed or merged. The change waits for the operator's review.\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:96:| Fix the trigger text, not the sk-doc router or the Gate 3 classifier | The router's `clarify` is correct for a note that no doc mode fits. The classifier returned `no_match` for the relaunch seed and for a read-only prompt, so it does not fire on this path |\n","metadata":{"output":"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"A session with no Gate 3 answer can now hand off near the context limit without an operator prompt. The spec gate exempts the gitignored handoff note, AGENTS.md says so in its gate sentences, and the repo OpenCode default model is pinned. Live run 10 proved the hop on Claude, Pi and OpenCode with zero operator prompts.\"\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:23:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:49:A session that has no Gate 3 answer can now hand off near its context limit and finish the work in a fresh session, with no operator prompt. Before this phase, two framework rules and one hook rule stopped the hop. The spec gate denied the write of the handoff note when enforcement was on and a gate was open. Gate 3 asked the operator before a read-only session wrote its note. The Gate 2 artifact trigger sent the note to sk-doc, which answered `clarify`.\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:53:The spec gate now treats a write under `.skilled/skills/.state/` as gitignored runtime state and lets it through. The one exception is a concern's tracked `README.md` directly under that folder, which stays gated, as does a `.state` folder nested under another path. The two AGENTS.md sentences that decide whether a turn is spec work now say the same thing, so a session reads the exemption before it decides to ask Gate 3 or to route the note to sk-doc.\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:63:| `AGENTS.md` | Modified | Gate 2 artifact trigger (line 70) and Gate 3 \"does not fire\" clause (line 75) name gitignored runtime state |\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:83:Live run 10 came last. Three loops ran in detached tmux sessions through `clean-tmux.sh`, with the Claude session variables and `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset. Each prompt carried no Gate 3 answer, and the thresholds were `SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD=0.05`, `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS=100` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS=1`. Each loop prepared, took SIGTERM, relaunched and declined a further hop. Nothing was committed, pushed or merged. The change waits for the operator's review.\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:96:| Fix the trigger text, not the sk-doc router or the Gate 3 classifier | The router's `clarify` is correct for a note that no doc mode fits. The classifier returned `no_match` for the relaunch seed and for a read-only prompt, so it does not fire on this path |\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"Gate 3\\|spec_folder\\|no answer\\|answered\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md | head -20","time":{"start":1792430668497,"end":1792430668509}},"id":"prt_155317a0e0012Rw7BQpWi4r9VG","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_15531581c001Ylx6ucCVIB7DNu"}}
