{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430688075,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_hoCMoQdbhhVJVdArKVgv3534","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"D77\\|transient \\`process.ppid\\`\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/003-command-trigger-runtimes/implementation-summary.md; grep -n \"Target the Stop hook's CLAUDE_PID\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md; grep -n \"D3 \\|claim seed carries\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/goal.md; grep -n \"wrapper-specific \\`process.ppid\\`\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/002-pi-opencode-adapters/implementation-summary.md"},"output":"86:SWE reviewed every diff that landed. D67 passed the arms. D72 failed the Codex adapter on one P0: `prepare` rejected `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME=codex`, which also broke `/speckit:handoff` on cursor, hermes and devin. D73 failed the Hermes adapter on two P1s: usage popped per message killed the nudge, and the same prepare rejection. D77 confirmed a further P1 in the fix (codex stop-arm targeted the transient `process.ppid`) plus a P2 that the manual claim command was wrong for hermes and opencode. D83 closed the loop: PASS with 0 P0 and 0 P1, a live `bash -c` probe proving the loop's direct child resolution, and end-to-end codex and hermes runs through prepare, arm, SIGTERM and `should-relaunch` true.\n145:2. **Carried P2 findings from the D77 and D83 reviews.** All eight were fixed later in the run, tests first: the Hermes window (D89), the own-property lookup and `!` escaping (D85, D91), the event-name gate and spawn-failure rule (D87), the runtime-neutral busy error (D86, D92), the pid miss, now printed and consumed by the wrapper on a pending exit (D91), and the unset-runtime default (D86, D93). The findings were:\n146:   - Hermes never reports the context window, so fill uses `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS` or the 200K default and a 128K model reads low (D77).\n95:| Target the Stop hook's CLAUDE_PID, falling back to its parent pid. | The killer is detached, so its own parent is not the Claude process. The loop-id ancestry check remains. Evidence: run-ledger.md, Design amendments from S1 and interface-contract.md, section 9. |\n49:| D3 | The handoff is a standalone note. When a spec packet is bound, `/speckit:save` runs before the hop, the claim seed carries the packet as the session's Gate 3 answer, and `/speckit:resume` runs after the claim. A sender that answered Gate 3 with Skip records `none`, and the seed carries that Skip. |\n121:| D3 amendment | Operator, 2026-10-17: \"Carry it in the seed\". Relaunched sessions stopped at Gate 3; the seed now carries the note's spec folder and AGENTS.md treats a hop as the same session |\n125:| D3 amendment 2 | Live Codex hop 2026-10-18: the sender answered Gate 3 Skip, the seed carried nothing and the receiver asked again; an explicit `none` now carries the Skip, and an empty field still asks |\n65:The spike verdicts are Pi 1.2.0 AUTO and OpenCode 1.19.0 AUTO (run-ledger D27 and `scratch/spike/SPIKE-REPORT.md`). The spike report keeps three limits visible: Pi TUI seed auto-send was source-verified but not exercised live, OpenCode TUI prompt auto-submit was not traced end to end and OpenCode `session.idle` on TUI quit plus wrapper-specific `process.ppid` were not directly captured.\n156:4. **Spike limits remain recorded.** Pi TUI seed submission and OpenCode TUI prompt submission were not end-to-end live-tested. OpenCode TUI quit behavior for `session.idle` and wrapper-specific `process.ppid` were not directly captured.\n","metadata":{"output":"86:SWE reviewed every diff that landed. D67 passed the arms. D72 failed the Codex adapter on one P0: `prepare` rejected `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME=codex`, which also broke `/speckit:handoff` on cursor, hermes and devin. D73 failed the Hermes adapter on two P1s: usage popped per message killed the nudge, and the same prepare rejection. D77 confirmed a further P1 in the fix (codex stop-arm targeted the transient `process.ppid`) plus a P2 that the manual claim command was wrong for hermes and opencode. D83 closed the loop: PASS with 0 P0 and 0 P1, a live `bash -c` probe proving the loop's direct child resolution, and end-to-end codex and hermes runs through prepare, arm, SIGTERM and `should-relaunch` true.\n145:2. **Carried P2 findings from the D77 and D83 reviews.** All eight were fixed later in the run, tests first: the Hermes window (D89), the own-property lookup and `!` escaping (D85, D91), the event-name gate and spawn-failure rule (D87), the runtime-neutral busy error (D86, D92), the pid miss, now printed and consumed by the wrapper on a pending exit (D91), and the unset-runtime default (D86, D93). The findings were:\n146:   - Hermes never reports the context window, so fill uses `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS` or the 200K default and a 128K model reads low (D77).\n95:| Target the Stop hook's CLAUDE_PID, falling back to its parent pid. | The killer is detached, so its own parent is not the Claude process. The loop-id ancestry check remains. Evidence: run-ledger.md, Design amendments from S1 and interface-contract.md, section 9. |\n49:| D3 | The handoff is a standalone note. When a spec packet is bound, `/speckit:save` runs before the hop, the claim seed carries the packet as the session's Gate 3 answer, and `/speckit:resume` runs after the claim. A sender that answered Gate 3 with Skip records `none`, and the seed carries that Skip. |\n121:| D3 amendment | Operator, 2026-10-17: \"Carry it in the seed\". Relaunched sessions stopped at Gate 3; the seed now carries the note's spec folder and AGENTS.md treats a hop as the same session |\n125:| D3 amendment 2 | Live Codex hop 2026-10-18: the sender answered Gate 3 Skip, the seed carried nothing and the receiver asked again; an explicit `none` now carries the Skip, and an empty field still asks |\n65:The spike verdicts are Pi 1.2.0 AUTO and OpenCode 1.19.0 AUTO (run-ledger D27 and `scratch/spike/SPIKE-REPORT.md`). The spike report keeps three limits visible: Pi TUI seed auto-send was source-verified but not exercised live, OpenCode TUI prompt auto-submit was not traced end to end and OpenCode `session.idle` on TUI quit plus wrapper-specific `process.ppid` were not directly captured.\n156:4. **Spike limits remain recorded.** Pi TUI seed submission and OpenCode TUI prompt submission were not end-to-end live-tested. OpenCode TUI quit behavior for `session.idle` and wrapper-specific `process.ppid` were not directly captured.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"D77\\|transient \\`process.ppid\\`\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/003-command-trigger-runtimes/implementation-summary.md; grep -n \"Target the Stop hook's CLAUDE_PID\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md; grep -n \"D3 \\|claim seed carries\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/goal.md; grep -n \"wrapper-specific \\`process.ppid\\`\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/002-pi-opencode-adapters/implementation-summary.md","time":{"start":1792430688043,"end":1792430688069}},"id":"prt_15531c557001R9C6XNuhVlxer0","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_15531a19800110LIxhYAiaMery"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430688245,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_8gTxh5BWefnaTJoWwZZQ8125","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"background_tasks\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs | head -10"},"output":"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md:80:| (a) Hook payload shapes | PostToolUse carries session_id, transcript_path, cwd, prompt_id, permission_mode, effort, hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input, tool_response, tool_use_id and duration_ms. Stop carries the shared session fields plus stop_hook_active, last_assistant_message, background_tasks (list) and session_crons (list). UserPromptSubmit carries the shared session fields plus prompt. None carries context size, tokens or a percentage. Evidence: run-ledger.md, D1 result and scratch/spike/SPIKE-REPORT.md. |\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md:96:| Check active work through shell ancestry and Stop background_tasks. | Plain pgrep would treat MCP child processes as active shell work. The two checks preserve those processes while refusing an active shell child or pending background task. Evidence: run-ledger.md, Design amendments from S1. |\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs:111:    && Array.isArray(payload.background_tasks)\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs:112:    && payload.background_tasks.length > 0\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs:117:      tasks: payload.background_tasks.length,\n","metadata":{"output":"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md:80:| (a) Hook payload shapes | PostToolUse carries session_id, transcript_path, cwd, prompt_id, permission_mode, effort, hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input, tool_response, tool_use_id and duration_ms. Stop carries the shared session fields plus stop_hook_active, last_assistant_message, background_tasks (list) and session_crons (list). UserPromptSubmit carries the shared session fields plus prompt. None carries context size, tokens or a percentage. Evidence: run-ledger.md, D1 result and scratch/spike/SPIKE-REPORT.md. |\nspecs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md:96:| Check active work through shell ancestry and Stop background_tasks. | Plain pgrep would treat MCP child processes as active shell work. The two checks preserve those processes while refusing an active shell child or pending background task. Evidence: run-ledger.md, Design amendments from S1. |\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs:111:    && Array.isArray(payload.background_tasks)\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs:112:    && payload.background_tasks.length > 0\n.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs:117:      tasks: payload.background_tasks.length,\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"background_tasks\" specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/001-claude-relaunch-loop/implementation-summary.md .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/stop-arm.mjs | head -10","time":{"start":1792430688232,"end":1792430688244}},"id":"prt_15531c7490015Rks2JbHcwQAWy","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_15531a19800110LIxhYAiaMery"}}
