{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792430963189,"sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_8iWA3trcQu1Lajauq0MH4777","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n 30,55p specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md; echo \"---STRATEGY NEXT---\"; grep -n \"NEXT FOCUS\" -A4 specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md | tail -8; echo \"---SYNTHESIS TAIL---\"; tail -2 specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:progress -->\n## 3. PROGRESS\n\n| # | Focus | Track | Ratio | Findings | Status |\n|---|-------|-------|-------|----------|--------|\n| 1 | Core relaunch state machine and process-targeting seams | - | 1.00 | 5 | complete |\n| 2 | Runtime adapter parity and untrusted spec-folder input | - | 0.90 | 5 | complete |\n| 3 | Command, README, catalog and environment-reference alignment | - | 0.90 | 5 | complete |\n| 4 | Phase 001-008 record drift against the current code | - | 0.80 | 4 | complete |\n| 5 | Ideal core-and-adapter boundary and standards conformance | - | 0.70 | 5 | complete |\n\n- iterationsCompleted: 5\n- keyFindings: 24\n- openQuestions: 1\n- resolvedQuestions: 4\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:progress -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 4. QUESTIONS\n- Answered: 4/5\n- [x] Which behaviors in `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib` and `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop` diverge from the phase 001-008 spec records, and which concrete fixes restore alignment?\n- [x] Do the runtime adapters (Claude, OpenCode plugin, Pi, Codex, Hermes) implement the same trigger, arm and nudge semantics as the core, and where do they drift?\n- [x] Does `/speckit:handoff`, its command documentation and the Gate 3 exemption match the implemented contract and the sk-doc standards?\n- [x] What is the ideal core-and-adapter architecture, and which sk-code-skilled surface checklist items and sk-doc standards remain unmet?\n- [ ] Which latent bugs and edge cases remain in the core relaunch decision path (context threshold, nudge, killer, handoff) and which tests expose them? [legacy-import]\n\n---STRATEGY NEXT---\n244:## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n245-Follow up on: **P3 — The tests README omits the OpenCode plugin suite from the folder inventory, so a reader cannot find one fifth of the regression coverage.** The README says the suite covers Claude, Codex, Hermes and Pi [SOURCE:...\n246-\n247-<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n248-\n---SYNTHESIS TAIL---\n\nThe highest-value next action is the A1/A2 target-resolution fix plus its test, followed by B1 and C1. The documentation corrections in G1-G7 can run in parallel because they touch no behavior. The structural move in F1 should follow the conformance suite so the suite can prove the move preserved behavior.\n","metadata":{"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:progress -->\n## 3. PROGRESS\n\n| # | Focus | Track | Ratio | Findings | Status |\n|---|-------|-------|-------|----------|--------|\n| 1 | Core relaunch state machine and process-targeting seams | - | 1.00 | 5 | complete |\n| 2 | Runtime adapter parity and untrusted spec-folder input | - | 0.90 | 5 | complete |\n| 3 | Command, README, catalog and environment-reference alignment | - | 0.90 | 5 | complete |\n| 4 | Phase 001-008 record drift against the current code | - | 0.80 | 4 | complete |\n| 5 | Ideal core-and-adapter boundary and standards conformance | - | 0.70 | 5 | complete |\n\n- iterationsCompleted: 5\n- keyFindings: 24\n- openQuestions: 1\n- resolvedQuestions: 4\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:progress -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 4. QUESTIONS\n- Answered: 4/5\n- [x] Which behaviors in `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib` and `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop` diverge from the phase 001-008 spec records, and which concrete fixes restore alignment?\n- [x] Do the runtime adapters (Claude, OpenCode plugin, Pi, Codex, Hermes) implement the same trigger, arm and nudge semantics as the core, and where do they drift?\n- [x] Does `/speckit:handoff`, its command documentation and the Gate 3 exemption match the implemented contract and the sk-doc standards?\n- [x] What is the ideal core-and-adapter architecture, and which sk-code-skilled surface checklist items and sk-doc standards remain unmet?\n- [ ] Which latent bugs and edge cases remain in the core relaunch decision path (context threshold, nudge, killer, handoff) and which tests expose them? [legacy-import]\n\n---STRATEGY NEXT---\n244:## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n245-Follow up on: **P3 — The tests README omits the OpenCode plugin suite from the folder inventory, so a reader cannot find one fifth of the regression coverage.** The README says the suite covers Claude, Codex, Hermes and Pi [SOURCE:...\n246-\n247-<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n248-\n---SYNTHESIS TAIL---\n\nThe highest-value next action is the A1/A2 target-resolution fix plus its test, followed by B1 and C1. The documentation corrections in G1-G7 can run in parallel because they touch no behavior. The structural move in F1 should follow the conformance suite so the suite can prove the move preserved behavior.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"sed -n 30,55p specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md; echo \"---STRATEGY NEXT---\"; grep -n \"NEXT FOCUS\" -A4 specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md | tail -8; echo \"---SYNTHESIS TAIL---\"; tail -2 specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md","time":{"start":1792430963127,"end":1792430963187}},"id":"prt_15535f719001GNk3pD3PrH0X5p","sessionID":"ses_eaada65b7ffeHiWlwBKhGghsv7","messageID":"msg_15535da1e001ysFawXdRdWF0Ga"}}
